    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Seattle-WA/MIE-Part-time-Lecturer--Aerospace-Program--Seattle-_R138997": {
      "title": "MIE Part-time Lecturer- Aerospace Program (Seattle)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-17\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary In person teaching of our undergraduate Aerospace minor core courses of Fluid Mechanics (ME3475), Introduction to flight (ME3465), and Aeronautical Propulsion (ME3470). Instructor will be responsible for their own class notes preparation, homework sets, quizzes, midterm exams, final exam, and grading of them. The instructor/s shall coordinator the coverage materials, assessments and textbooks with Thermofluids group coordinator or their representative.   Upon consideration of Thermofluids group coordinator, if logistics allow the lectures and assessments will be synced with Boston campus. Minimum Qualifications PhD in Mechanical Engineering with Thermo-Science concentration. Clear understanding of the undergraduate fluid mechanics. First seven chapters of Frank White textbook could be used as a guide. Experience and clear understanding of Aerospace system design, including Aerodynamics of flight and propulsion system. Experience with classroom teaching. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Class notes preparation and class teaching time. Office hours. Homework, quiz, and exam preparation. Homework, quiz, and exam grading. Weekly/periodic coordination meeting with Boston campus representative/instructors. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: per credit rate is $2693.75"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Part-Time-Lecturer---Department-of-Public-Health-and-Health-Sciences--Boston-Campus-_R142986": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer - Department of Public Health and Health Sciences (Boston Campus)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Opportunity  The Department of Public Health and Health Sciences in the Bouvé College of Health Sciences of Northeastern University is hiring part-time lecturers for the 26-27 academic year on the Boston campus.   The Department’s mission is to promote the health and well-being of diverse individuals, communities, and populations through health care innovations and interdisciplinary collaborative initiatives across all scientific fields, engineering, and the humanities. The Department and the College are strongly committed to fostering excellence through diversity and enthusiastically welcome nominations and applications from members of groups that have been, and continue to be, underrepresented in academia.   Responsibilities include:  Preparing syllabi, lectures, course materials, all examinations including a final exam, and evaluations of student performance in the course; Developing and implementing materials for lectures for in-person or online/hybrid courses. Working under the direction of the Lead Faculty; Holding office hours as appropriate; Engaging productively with teaching assistants; Collaborating on course revisions and improvements with department faculty and the University’s Center for the Advancement of Teaching and Learning through Research (CATLR).  Representative Courses   PHTH 2515. Healthcare Policy and Administration.      This course focuses on management and policy issues in healthcare. Discusses management and administrative structures in hospitals and other healthcare organizations, including community clinics and health organizations, both private and public. Introduces the financial systems, economic information, and payment mechanisms necessary to understand healthcare financing. Also explores the variety of factors that influence population health from a healthcare policy perspective. Offers students an opportunity to learn how to analyze, prepare, and write policy briefs based on understanding the various economic, legal, and political forces shaping healthcare in the United States.     PHTH 4202. Principles of Epidemiology in Medicine and Public Health.    This course introduces the principles of epidemiology necessary to critically evaluate the published research in medicine, public health, and related fields. Through careful reading of literature, class discussion, and lectures, familiarizes students with the study of design-related considerations that are an indispensable part of interpreting scientific literature. Offers students an opportunity to learn how to recognize critical elements of research design and execution (e.g., loss to follow-up in randomized clinical trials and other cohort designs, selection bias in case control studies, etc.); identify the strengths and limitations of different approaches to research questions; deepen their understanding of causal inference; and recognize the provisional nature of scientific knowledge. It covers issues of statistical methods and data analysis; however, there are no computational requirements.  Qualifications:   Applicants should have at least a Masters in an appropriate field. Doctoral degrees and teaching experience are preferred.   Application:   Please provide a CV/resume and a cover letter that includes description of qualifications and Public Health/Health Sciences course you are prepared to teach.  Position Type:   Academic  Additional Information:   Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.  We do not offer visa sponsorship for this role and are looking for candidates who are already authorized to work in the United States without sponsorship.  Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.     Northeastern University is an equal opportunity employer, seeking to recruit and support a broadly diverse community of faculty and staff.  Northeastern values and celebrates diversity in all its forms and strives to foster an inclusive culture built on respect that affirms inter-group relations and builds cohesion.   All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.  To learn more about Northeastern University’s commitment and support of diversity and inclusion, please see www.northeastern.edu/diversity .  Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The pay rate per credit is $2085.00."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Senior-Program-Operations-Manager_R142982": {
      "title": "Senior Program Operations Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary: The Senior Program Operations Manager plays a key role in ensuring the efficient planning, implementation, and management of operational processes within the online learning unit. Possessing strong operational, technical, and interpersonal skills this role focuses on streamlining workflows, supporting program launches, student tracking, and collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality online learning experiences. The ideal candidate thrives in a fast-paced environment, is highly organized, and demonstrates a commitment to excellence in higher education.   Key Accountabilities & Responsibilities: Program Operations Management: Oversee the end-to-end operational processes for online learning programs, including year-long class schedules and semester task tracking. Lead semesterly ready to launch initiatives in collaboration with Program & Relationship Managers flagging enrollment or course build issues. Work with Program and Relationship Managers to track and ensure timely processing of faculty contracts for development projects, and teaching. Process student matriculation each term including tracking materials and conducting student outreach. Monitor key performance indicators (KPIs) related to program operations and provide regular reports to leadership Manage students lists for student events, welcome packets, MailChimp, advising etc. Review and flag issues with student records, including student attributes, modality, scholarships, or course registration. Develop and document standard operating procedures (SOPs) and program handbooks/manuals to ensure consistency and efficiency across all programs. Oversee semesterly data clean up process to ensure most accurate student lists.\" This includes inactivating learners with the Registrar Learner Experience Support: Monitor and improve operational touchpoints to ensure learner satisfaction and retention. Act as team lead on Navigate 360, Stellic, and Help Scout initiatives. Support non-credit course delivery by setting up Canvas announcements and provide student inbox support as needed. Support for-credit course delivery by creating synchronous sessions via Teams/Zoom and maintaining attendance data. Creating course pack links for for-credit courses. Creating and adding Panopto playlists for for-credit courses   Collaboration and Stakeholder Management: Identify opportunities to streamline workflows, enhance systems, and improve the scalability of program operations. Stay informed of emerging trends, technologies, and best practices in online learning operations. Collaborate with external vendors or partners to support technology implementation, course production, or learner engagement initiatives. Lead or support process improvement initiatives to align operations with strategic goals. Other projects and responsibilities as needed Contribute to positive team culture and collaborate effectively with program team, learning design team, and business partners. Take feedback from team members and clients and find the best ways to address concerns and provide new solutions. Act as a team player and pitch-in wherever help is needed, including supporting management of program projects, communication across teams, and mentoring others as needed. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in education, business administration, or a related field required. Master’s degree preferred. Minimum 3-5 years of experience in operations management, preferably in higher education or online learning.\\ Proven success managing complex projects and cross-functional teams. Strong organizational and project management skills with attention to detail. Ability to navigate ambiguity and adapt to changing priorities in a dynamic environment. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and collaboration skills. Familiarity with learning management systems (LMS), student information systems (SIS), and related technologies. Data-driven mindset with the ability to analyze metrics and inform decision-making. Experience working in a highly collaborative environment and promoting a teamwork mentality. High level of initiative and drive with a strong sense of urgency and accountability. Ability to work independently, but also as a team member when the situation warrants. Ability to solve problems, analyze learner survey and performance data and synthesize and summarize information. Consistently looks for a better way to do things in order to create organizational efficiency and effectiveness. Acts as a good steward of the university’s resources. Smartsheet experience preferred Familiarity with Slate and Banner (or similar CRM/SIS platforms) Experience collaborating with higher education units such as Enrollment Management, ITS, and the Registrar Position Type Academic Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 108S Expected Hiring Range: $60,315.00 - $85,192.50 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Arlington-VA/Part-Time-Lecturer---Analytics--Arlington-_R142996": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer - Analytics (Arlington)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Professional Studies at Northeastern University invites applications for a non-tenure track part time faculty lecturer in Analytics on the Arlington campus. The College of Professional Studies is one of ten colleges of Northeastern University, a nationally ranked private research university. Founded in 1960, the College provides lifelong experiential learning that unleashes the capacities of aspiring individuals in all stages and walks of life. The College teaches undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students on campus and online in more than 90 programs.  Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa . Responsibilities Qualified candidates must be prepared to work with global student populations. Instructional areas included, but are not limited to, analytics, with particular expertise in probability and statistics, data exploration, data visualization, , database management systems, leadership and risk management in analytics, business support and predictive analytics. The mission of the Master of Professional Studies in Analytics program is to foster foundational analytics skills among working professionals, including preparing data, conducting data analysis, forecasting, optimization, data visualization, and data storytelling. This degree prepares students for entry and mid-level roles in analytics, such as data analyst, data specialist, database analyst, program analyst, research analyst, or research associate. These roles are general analyst roles and are not specific to any particular professional domains or disciplines (e.g., business, marketing, and engineering). The degree is deeply rooted in experiential learning that is closely linked to professional applications in the workforce. Qualifications Masters in an aligned discipline and analytics-industry experience. Preference for candidates with a PhD in a sciences field, or similar. Demonstration of teaching, coaching, and/or training is required, with a history of successful teaching (online/on ground) at the graduate level is strongly preferred. Application Materials Applicants should submit materials including a cover letter and vitae. Successful faculty at Northeastern will be dynamic and innovative scholars with a record of teaching excellence and a commitment to fostering belonging in the university community. Thus, strong candidates for this faculty position will have the expertise, knowledge, and skills to build their pedagogy, and curriculum in ways that reflect and enhance this commitment. Please indicate how your expertise, knowledge, and skills have prepared you to contribute to this work in your cover letter. Please direct questions to Joe Reilly at j.reilly@northeastern.edu. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,086.44."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Elma-Lewis-Digital-Project-Assistant_R142919": {
      "title": "Elma Lewis Digital Project Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About Northeastern University Library The Northeastern University Library is hiring part-time assistants for a grant-funded project supported by Boston’s Community Preservation Department. The project, Black Art and Joy in Boston (and Beyond): Elma Lewis and the National Center of Afro-American Artists, focuses on digitizing, cataloging, and publishing materials from four archival collections documenting the life and legacy of Elma Lewis (1921–2004). These collections include her personal papers, as well as records from the Elma Lewis School of Fine Arts, the National Center of Afro-American Artists, and its museum, highlighting her work to promote Afrocentric visual and performing arts. Job Summary Part-time assistants will contribute to the descriptive work for the Elma Lewis collections, with assignments determined by project priorities. The assistant will work within the highly collaborative Digital Production Services department and also partner with staff from Archives and Special Collections. Hours: 15–18 hours a week. Location: Hybrid and fully remote work available. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Catalog textual materials in spreadsheets according to departmental standards and project-specific instructions from the Project Librarian Additional tasks may include: Perform post-production processing of digitized texts Assist with automated captioning workflows for audiovisual materials Develop contextual documentation about the people, places, and objects represented in the collections Minimum Qualifications Required Some experience with metadata creation Demonstrated interest in inclusive cataloging and reparative description Strong attention to detail Ability to thrive in a collaborative environment Preferred Enrollment in an American Library Association (ALA)-accredited Master of Library Science (MLS) or Master of Library and Information Science (MLIS), or equivalent experience Professional experience with metadata schemas and item-level archival cataloging Experience using Metadata Object Description Schema (MODS), Dublin Core, or Encoded Archival Description (EAD) Familiarity with authority files and controlled vocabularies, such as Library of Congress Subject Headings (LCSH), Library of Congress Name Authority File (LCNAF), and Art & Architecture Thesaurus (AAT) Knowledge of controlled vocabularies and thesauri Exposure to inclusive and reparative description principles Proven ability to work independently Strong communication skills Required Documents Resume Position Type Temporary Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. This job is for a current or anticipated job vacancy. Pay Rate: $21/hour"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Temporary-Lab-Instructor_R142548-1": {
      "title": "Temporary Lab Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary Standardized Patients/Patient Actors assist with pharmacy and medical simulation labs in the Bouve College of Health Sciences. Through patient-provider role-playing, Standardized Patients enable health professions students to practice necessary skills and behaviors in labs and other simulated learning experiences. Standardized Patients must be on campus during scheduled times. They are utilized during the fall, spring, and summer terms, typically between 8:00 a.m. and 6:00 p.m., Monday through Friday. Standardized Patients may be scheduled to work one or multiple activities and typically work between two and eight hours during an activity. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Assist with pharmacy and medical simulation labs in the Bouve College of Health Sciences Portray all the characteristics of a real patient Simulate specific emotions, behaviors, and disease symptoms Engage in patient-provider role-playing with health professions students Minimum Qualifications Required Excellent English oral and written communication skills Excellent attention to detail Ability to recall case information as cued by students in role-play situations Ability to solve problems and work well under pressure Willingness to work an intermittent schedule as needed Required Documents Resume Position Type Temporary Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. This job is for a current or anticipated job vacancy. Pay Rate: $30/hour"
