    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Vancouver-BC-Canada/Customer-Service---Campus-Operations-Assistant_R142896": {
      "title": "Customer Service & Campus Operations Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity This is a temporary position filling a leave of absence, with a possibility of extension. Qualifications  The ideal candidate will have a minimum of two years of office coordination experience. Experience in higher education is a plus. The candidate must enjoy working with diverse populations and be comfortable working independently. The successful candidate will have outstanding customer service and interpersonal skills, and proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and G Suite. Experience with AI tools, like Claude or CoPilot are preferred. Detail oriented with a focus on quality and accuracy is desired. Must be able to learn quickly in a technical environment, and operate video conferencing equipment, printers, copiers, and computers. Flexibility, a positive attitude, and commitment to excellence are vital. Duties & Responsibilities Key point of contact: 35 % acting as the first point of contact for students and faculty ensuring that classes and campus activities are set up for success acting as a liaison and providing hospitality to incoming visitors which could include students and staff from other locations, business partners, and prospective students ensuring that campus amenities are fully supported and available to the community Campus operations and event support: 30 % troubleshooting technical issues and assisting with classroom technology; assisting with room setup, breakdown, and reconfiguration; assisting with student orientations and campus events; ensuring facility related issues are reported and followed up on in a timely fashion Completing administrative duties: 35 % including but not limited to assisting faculty and student services staff with printing handouts and organizing promotional materials; maintaining the campus areas in a clean and stocked manner; administration support to regulatory submission and review processes; administrative support relevant to campus operations, safety protocols, and University policies and procedures; special projects as assigned Our campus hours are currently 8:00 am to 9:00 pm and this position may alternate between evening shifts and day shifts to ensure campus coverage and to support events. Weekend shifts may also be required.        Position Type General Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 105H Expected Hiring Range: $24.51 - $36.77 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change.   Applicant must be legally entitled to work in Canada for the duration of the appointment or employment without employer sponsorship."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Portland-ME/Head-of-Business-Development---Industry-Partner-Programs_R142958": {
      "title": "Head of Business Development — Industry Partner Programs",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary: Founded in 1898, Northeastern University is renowned for our experiential learning model, high-impact research, deep partnerships, and worldwide reach. From day one, we've pursued innovative ways of teaching and research that place a premium on experience and engagement with the world. Today, our signature approach erases traditional boundaries, empowering not only students, but faculty, alumni, partners, and innovators to solve problems and pursue impact. We've created a one-of-a-kind global university system of 14 campuses, 49 alumni communities, and 3,900+ employer partners that forms a dynamic international community. We create new opportunities for richer educational experiences and deeper collaborations across industries and disciplines to bring the right expertise together to go from promise to reality. Northeastern University's Roux Institute is a global engine of innovation, talent-building, and economic growth in Portland, Maine. In 2020, Northeastern University partnered with David and Barbara Roux and the Harold Alfond Foundation to create the Roux Institute. Leveraging Northeastern's global University system, the Roux Institute positions Portland as a major innovation hub in AI, data science, and life sciences. This role works with a team based at the Roux Institute but with a global remit to bring the right programs to partners regardless of where the programs sit within the University. About the Opportunity: This is a build role. You will design, launch, and scale the growth strategy for Industry Partner Programs run out of the Roux Institute and the Institute for Experiential AI, and lead the teams that turn partner relationships into lasting impact. The Roux Institute was built on an ethos of listening to our partners and creating offerings that can meet them where they are today and help them envision where they might go in the future. Our partners span companies of every size and industry vertical. Getting the structure and the people right, so every partner gets a team that understands their world, is the single biggest determinant of your success in this role. You'll also carry a personal revenue target and a portfolio of your own partner relationships. Our strongest BD leader needs to be in the room for our most important partnerships, modeling what a great partner experience looks like and staying close enough to the work to keep the team's playbook current. The person who thrives here operates at two altitudes at once: strategic enough to set direction, tactical enough to close the engagement and build durable, flexible partnerships that can adapt over time. You understand the impact of data and AI across industries well enough to hold your own with a CEO, CTO and a CFO and you know how to listen and elicit partner priorities to meet a real partner need. You build a culture that's curious, humble, fast, data-driven, accountable, and partner-obsessed. Continuous improvement is one of your core values. You will manage 3-6 direct reports and lead a broader team of 9-12, spanning business development, partnership operations, and demand generation. Core Responsibilities Build and lead a high-performing, partner-obsessed sales organization: set performance targets, build the funnel, define sales motions, and own engagement attribution. Set strategic direction for how we go to market: product and service positioning, target partner development, messaging, and ICP refinement. Personally own and grow a portfolio of strategic partner relationships, serving as a trusted advisor as much as a dealmaker. The successful candidate will bring the following qualifications, experience, skills, and dispositions to the role. Required Qualifications Education Bachelor's degree required; advanced degree preferred. Experience 10+ years of B2B solution selling in advanced technology, ideally data or AI products and services. A track record of building and scaling high-performing sales teams from the ground up. A track record of personally closing revenue-generating deals with sophisticated B2B buyers. Skills and Dispositions Proven ability to recruit, coach, and scale top sales and BD talent. Skilled at building trust with partner stakeholders and internal alliances, and navigating politics within large, complex organizations. Comfortable operating with startup-level speed, ambiguity, and resourcefulness. Communicates with precision, backed by data, dashboards, and forecasts. Fluent in budgeting, forecasting, and running operations inside a complex organization. Proficient with modern sales tools (e.g., Salesforce). Demonstrated history of hitting revenue targets in a B2B sales environment. Takes full ownership of outcomes, both personal and team-wide. Curiosity is essential for this role. The successful candidate will be confident and capable but will approach the work with humility and a learning mindset. Location Portland, Maine preferred. Other Northeastern campus locations will be considered. This is a mostly in-person role with some flexibility to work remotely. Position Type General Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 114S Expected Hiring Range: $130,945.00 - $189,868.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Charlotte-NC/Part-Time-Lecturer---School-of-Nursing--Charlotte--NC_R142963": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer - School of Nursing, Charlotte, NC",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity School of Nursing Part-time Lecturer positions are available to teach online and at clinical sites for our Charlotte, North Carolina campus in the following areas: Adult Medical/Surgical, Community Health, Maternal Child/Women's Health, Pediatric, and Psychiatric Nursing. Responsibilities for clinical site instruction include providing opportunities for student learning, assessing and evaluating student performance, and collaborating with clinical course coordinators to prepare students for practice. Responsibilities for didactic instruction include: preparation of lectures, course materials, examinations, and evaluation of student performance in the course with the Course Lead Faculty. Part-time Lecturer positions are available as determined by the School's curricular and institutional needs. Part-time instructors will work under the direction of the Course Lead Faculty for the course and will hold weekly office hours. Start dates: May, September, and January. Qualifications: Requirements for online teaching include a Master's degree in an appropriate healthcare-related discipline as well as recent experience in practice. Requirements for clinical instruction include a Master's degree in Nursing, two years' experience in the clinical specialty, and unrestricted RN licensure in North Carolina. Successful applicants will have significant career accomplishments within subject area and college teaching experience in large, diverse higher education institutions. Salary dependent upon teaching assignment. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $1395"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Part-Time-Lecturer---American-Sign-Language-and-Interpreting-Education_R142909": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer - American Sign Language and Interpreting Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Social Sciences and Humanities and its nine tenure units are the home of the Experiential Liberal Arts. Through its research, teaching, and engagement missions, the college collaborates across the university, the Northeastern network, and partners around the globe.    Responsibilities: The American Sign Language Program seeks candidates to teach undergraduate courses such as ASL, deaf culture, history, or literature and linguistics courses.   Positions are available throughout the year contingent upon enrollment and departmental need. Qualifications: Master’s degree in a related field strongly preferred. Fluency in American Sign Languages required. ASLTA or RID-certified strongly preferred. Three to five years of teaching experience in ASL, or interpreting strongly preferred. Cross-cultural understanding and excellent communication skills required.   Documents to Submit: CV and Cover Letter required. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,085."
