    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Research-Technician---Antibiotic-Discovery-Center_R142931": {
      "title": "Research Technician - Antibiotic Discovery Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Antibiotic Discovery Center (ADC) The Antibiotic Discovery Center (ADC) at Northeastern University is an interdisciplinary research hub dedicated to discovering, characterizing, and developing novel antibiotics and bioactive natural products. The ADC integrates expertise in microbiology, biochemistry, chemical biology, and natural product chemistry to address the urgent global challenge of antimicrobial resistance. Researchers at the ADC work collaboratively to identify new compounds from diverse microbial sources, elucidate their mechanisms of action, and advance them toward preclinical development through innovative screening, analytical, and genomic approaches. Job Summary The ADC is seeking a motivated Research Technician to assist in natural product-based antibiotic discovery. The successful candidate will support the preparation, execution, and analysis of microbiological and biochemical experiments, contributing to research on the identification and characterization of novel bioactive compounds. This position offers an excellent opportunity for recent graduates to gain hands-on experience in an active research environment. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Assist with routine microbiological and biochemical experiments to support ongoing discovery projects. Culture and maintain bacterial strains and prepare media, buffers, and reagents. Perform basic assays to evaluate compound activity under supervision. Support compound extraction, purification, and sample preparation for analysis. Maintain accurate laboratory notebooks and assist with data organization and entry. Contribute to general laboratory maintenance, including supply inventory and equipment upkeep. Collaborate closely with senior laboratory members to learn new experimental techniques. Minimum Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree in Microbiology, Biochemistry, Chemistry, Molecular Biology, or a related field. Basic understanding of microbial culture, molecular biology, or biochemical assays. Strong attention to detail, organizational skills, and eagerness to learn. Ability to work both independently and as part of a collaborative research team. Preferred Prior laboratory experience, including academic or internship-based experience. Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 105H Expected Hiring Range: $20.77 - $28.56 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Sr-Research-Technician---Antibiotic-Discovery-Center_R142930-1": {
      "title": "Sr. Research Technician - Antibiotic Discovery Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary The Antibiotic Discovery Center (ADC) at Northeastern University is seeking a highly motivated Senior Research Technician to support the development and implementation of a target-based screening platform for antibiotic discovery, assist in downstream hit validation and compound isolation, and contribute to overall laboratory operations in a collaborative research environment. Responsibilities Contribute to development of a novel microfluidics-based high-throughput screening platform Execute biochemical and microbiological assays to identify and validate antibacterial targets. Support high-throughput and focused screening efforts, including assay development, optimization, and data analysis. Participate in hit triage, secondary assays, and compound characterization, including natural product isolation and structure–activity studies. Operate and maintain equipment supporting screening and compound purification (e.g., LC, HPLC, plate readers, microfluidics sorters). Manage lab inventories, supplies, and safety compliance; coordinate maintenance and calibration of shared instruments. Contribute to protocol development, data management, and preparation of reports and presentations. Provide training and technical support to students and new lab members.   Qualifications Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Microbiology, Biochemistry, Chemistry, Molecular Biology, or a related field. Minimum 2–3 years of hands-on research experience in an academic or industrial setting. Technical expertise in molecular cloning, bacterial culture, and biochemical or enzymatic assays. Experience with natural product extraction, chromatographic purification, or analytical instrumentation (e.g., LC-MS) is strongly preferred. Strong organizational and communication skills, with the ability to multitask in a dynamic research environment.   Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 108H Expected Hiring Range: $29.00 - $40.96 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Oakland-CA/Adjunct-Faculty---Music_R139803": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Music",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Summary and Responsibility The Department of Music in the College of Arts, Media and Design, Northeastern University seeks adjunct faculty to teach courses on a variety of Music related topics in our Oakland campus.  Qualifications PhD is preferred or equivalent professional experience. Previous teaching experience at the college level and a broad knowledge of Humanities is highly desirable. Please note: applications are reviewed on a rolling basis.  Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,484.48."
