    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Vertex---Early-Development-Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow_R142352": {
      "title": "Vertex – Early Development Postdoctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Opportunity Northeastern University Pharmaceutical Industry Fellowships Program is a two-year experiential program designed to advance lifelong learning and the education and training of Pharm.D. graduates. A key element of the program’s success is preparing Fellows to meet evolving workforce needs across various sectors of the pharmaceutical industry. Fellows have the opportunity to work closely with our innovative biopharmaceutical industry partners, while engaging with Northeastern University faculty in professional and career development, teaching, service, and scholarly activities. In partnership with Northeastern University, Vertex Pharmaceuticals is offering a two-year Early Development fellowship, based in Boston, MA. About Vertex Pharmaceuticals Vertex is a global biotechnology company that invests in scientific innovation to create transformative medicines for people with serious diseases. The company has approved medicines that treat the underlying causes of multiple chronic, life-shortening genetic diseases — cystic fibrosis, sickle cell disease and transfusion-dependent beta thalassemia — and continues to advance clinical and research programs in these diseases. Vertex also has a robust clinical pipeline of investigational therapies across a range of modalities in other serious diseases where it has deep insight into causal human biology, including IgA nephropathy, neuropathic pain, APOL1-mediated kidney disease, primary membranous nephropathy, autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease, type 1 diabetes, and myotonic dystrophy type 1. Vertex was founded in 1989 and has its global headquarters in Boston, with international headquarters in London. Additionally, the company has research and development sites and commercial offices in North America, Europe, Australia, Latin America and the Middle East. Vertex is consistently recognized as one of the industry's top places to work, including 16 consecutive years on Science magazine's Top Employers list and one of Fortune’s 100 Best Companies to Work For. For company updates and to learn more about Vertex's history of innovation, visit www.vrtx.com or follow us on LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube and Twitter/X. Responsibilities Early Development Fellowship Description: Early Development comprises Clinical Pharmacology (CP), Modeling & Simulations (M&S), and Early Development Medical Directors (EDMD). CP provides pharmacokinetic (PK) and pharmacodynamic (PD) expertise. M&S provides model-driven PK and PK/PD quantitative pharmacology expertise. EDMD leads early clinical strategies and provides expertise in translating investigational therapies into first-in-human trials, whether they are healthy volunteers or patients. Vertex provides a structured 2-year fellowship program involving three rotations across Clinical Pharmacology, Modeling and Simulation, and Early Development Medical spanning different phases of development. Throughout the program, Early Development fellows will participate in relevant project strategy planning and development, analyze and interpret clinical trial results, and train on software utilized within the department (e.g., NONMEM, R, or Phoenix WinNonlin). The objectives specific to each rotation include: Clinical Pharmacology Rotation: • Design and lead clinical pharmacology studies (first-in-human, bioavailability, drug-drug interaction, immunogenicity) • Serve as clinical pharmacology lead and provide clinical trial operations support • Conduct noncompartmental PK analysis • Author clinical pharmacology sections of clinical study reports and provide support to regulatory documents Modeling and Simulation Rotation: • Implement model informed drug development (MIDD) using quantitative approaches (e.g., population PK, PK/PD, optimal sample design) to address critical questions during drug development • Contribute to M&S plans and/or translational medicine/clinical development plans • Conduct modeling and simulation activities to aid in the design and conduct of clinical trials (e.g., dose selection, sample collection) • Author M&S reports and/or regulatory documents in support of regulatory submissions Early Development, Medical Rotation: • Support design and execution of first-in-human studies (healthy volunteer or patient) • Contribute to design of early proof of mechanism (POM) strategies and studies • Contribute to design and execution of drug-drug interaction, ADME, TQT, and special population studies (hepatic and renal impairment) • Contribute to biomarker strategy development • Assist in updating investigator brochures and developing labeling language based on Phase 1 study results Qualifications • Doctor of Pharmacy degree from an ACPE-accredited institution • Eligible for pharmacist licensure in the State of Massachusetts • Excellent oral and written communication skills • Strong time management and leadership abilities • Ability to work independently and take initiative on a variety of projects at both the industry site and Northeastern Additional Information Applicants should submit the following application materials by the priority deadline of October 31, 2026. 1. Curriculum vitae (CV), uploaded 2. Unofficial PharmD transcripts, uploaded 3. Cover letter, uploaded Letters of Recommendation Three formal Letters of Recommendation (LORs) must be submitted directly by the letter writers no later than November 23, 2026 . Each letter writer must include: ·       The candidate's full name ·       The fellowship program(s) to which the candidate is applying (e.g., Smith, John – Alnylam, GSK ) Please ask your letter writers to complete and submit the Letter of Recommendation Form along with their recommendation. Click here to access the form and share it with your letter writers. Recommendations must be submitted directly by the recommender and cannot be submitted by the applicant. Address cover letter and letters of recommendation to: J. Andrew Orr-Skirvin, PharmD, BCOP Clinical Professor, Department of Pharmacy & Health Systems Sciences Pharmaceutical Industry Fellowship Program Director 360 Huntington Ave, 140 The Fenway R218 Boston, MA 02115 Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future.  STEM OPT is not compatible for this position. The successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University's sponsorship for a visa.  Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 108S Expected Hiring Range: $60,315.00 - $85,192.50 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Vertex---Market-Access-Strategy-Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow_R142357": {
      "title": "Vertex – Market Access Strategy Postdoctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Opportunity Northeastern University Pharmaceutical Industry Fellowships Program is a two-year experiential program designed to advance lifelong learning and the education and training of Pharm.D. graduates. A key element of the program’s success is preparing Fellows to meet evolving workforce needs across various sectors of the pharmaceutical industry. Fellows have the opportunity to work closely with our innovative biopharmaceutical industry partners, while engaging with Northeastern University faculty in professional and career development, teaching, service, and scholarly activities. In partnership with Northeastern University, Vertex Pharmaceuticals is offering a two-year North American Commercial—US Market Access Strategy fellowship, based in Boston, MA. About Vertex Pharmaceuticals Vertex is a global biotechnology company that invests in scientific innovation to create transformative medicines for people with serious diseases and conditions. The company has approved therapies for cystic fibrosis, sickle cell disease, transfusion-dependent beta thalassemia and acute pain, and it continues to advance clinical and research programs in these areas. Vertex also has a robust clinical pipeline of investigational therapies across a range of modalities in other serious diseases where it has deep insight into causal human biology, including IgA nephropathy, neuropathic pain, APOL1-mediated kidney disease, primary membranous nephropathy, autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease, type 1 diabetes, generalized myasthenia gravis, and myotonic dystrophy type 1. Vertex was founded in 1989 and has its global headquarters in Boston, with international headquarters in London. Additionally, the company has research and development sites and commercial offices in North America, Europe, Australia, Latin America and the Middle East. Vertex is consistently recognized as one of the industry's top places to work, including 16 consecutive years on Science magazine's Top Employers list and one of Fortune’s 100 Best Companies to Work For. For company updates and to learn more about Vertex's history of innovation, visit www.vrtx.com or follow us on LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube and X. Responsibilities US Market Access Strategy The U.S. Market Access Strategy position offers the opportunity to support payer marketing and strategy across the Vertex commercial and pipeline portfolio. The fellow will contribute to launch and lifecycle access planning as part of the Market Access Strategy team and will collaborate closely with cross-functional partners in Pricing and Contracting, HEOR, Public Affairs, and Brand Marketing. Through this work, the fellow will develop an understanding of how the company assesses market dynamics, evaluates access opportunities and barriers, and shapes value-based strategies to support patient access and payer engagement. Build foundational knowledge of U.S. market access strategy, including how payer, policy, reimbursement, and stakeholder dynamics influence access planning across products Advance strategic and tactical projects that strengthen launch and lifecycle market access planning in key disease areas that may include Type 1 Diabetes, Pain, IgA Nephropathy, APOL1-Mediated Kidney Disease, and Cystic Fibrosis Identify and explore innovative partnerships, market disruptors, and policy changes that may enhance compliant patient access and payer engagement Gain exposure to the regulatory and compliance environment, including CMS policies, state-specific regulations, and legal considerations surrounding access communications and contracting Contribute to the development of payer value propositions, access narratives, and strategic recommendations that support reimbursement, coverage optimization, and differentiated product positioning Create educational materials and resources that communicate market access strategy to internal and external stakeholders Qualifications Doctor of Pharmacy degree from an ACPE-accredited institution Eligible for pharmacist licensure in the State of Massachusetts Excellent oral and written communication skills Strong time management and leadership abilities Ability to work independently and take initiative on a variety of projects at both the industry site and Northeastern Preferred Candidate Traits : Demonstrated interest in US payer policy, market access strategy, and health economics Familiarity with the US healthcare system, including formulary decision-making processes and the evolving payer landscape Proven ability to manage multiple projects with strategic focus and attention to detail Self-starter with a learning mindset, business acumen and agility to thrive in a fast-paced, launch-oriented environment Additional Information Applicants should submit the following application materials by the priority deadline of October 31, 2026. 1. Curriculum vitae (CV), uploaded 2. Unofficial PharmD transcripts, uploaded 3. Cover letter, uploaded Letters of Recommendation Three formal Letters of Recommendation (LORs) must be submitted directly by the letter writers no later than November 23, 2026 . Each letter writer must include: ·       The candidate's full name ·       The fellowship program(s) to which the candidate is applying (e.g., Smith, John – Alnylam, GSK ) Please ask your letter writers to complete and submit the Letter of Recommendation Form along with their recommendation. Click here to access the form and share it with your letter writers. Recommendations must be submitted directly by the recommender and cannot be submitted by the applicant. Address cover letter and letters of recommendation to: J. Andrew Orr-Skirvin, PharmD, BCOP Clinical Professor, Department of Pharmacy & Health Systems Sciences Pharmaceutical Industry Fellowship Program Director 360 Huntington Ave, 140 The Fenway R218 Boston, MA 02115 Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future.  STEM OPT is not compatible for this position. The successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University's sponsorship for a visa.  Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 108S Expected Hiring Range: $60,315.00 - $85,192.50 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
