      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-29\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity JOB SUMMARY:    Fitness Center workers and Building Supervisors provide supervision to all users of the fitness center, gymnasium, activity rooms, tennis courts, and soccer field.   Team members ensure that all safety and emergency protocols are followed.   *This job position is located on the Oakland Campus and cannot be done remotely.      RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE:   Team members must be punctual, reliable, responsible, outgoing, and enjoy working with the public   Arrive to work on time, wearing appropriate attire to perform duties.   Communicate absences in advance and take initiative to find coverage.   Follow procedures for opening and closing the facilities.   Greet students/staff and faculty as they enter and exit the facility; assist them with any questions or concerns as they check in.   Ensure that patrons follow policies and redirect, as needed.   Maintain a professional demeanor during scheduled shift.   Resolve concerns and escalate to supervisor, as needed.   Answer phones in a friendly manner and assist callers with their inquiries.   Provide regular, consistent cleaning and sanitizing of all exercise equipment.   Do laundry, sweeping, vacuuming, mopping; follow specific cleaning protocols.   Frequently perform a comprehensive walk through of all facility areas (fitness center, activity rooms, gymnasium, tennis courts, soccer field); quickly fix or report any safety/policy issues and address cleanliness concerns.   Take initiative to ensure safety in the facility. Promptly report maintenance and facility concerns such as broken and/or missing equipment or unsafe conditions.   Anticipate, recognize, and react to all emergencies, and provide necessary, reporting to direct supervisor. Respond to all emergencies and follow procedures in the Emergency Action Plan.   Follow all policies and procedures set forth in the staff handbook.   Perform other admin/clerical duties as assigned by Campus Recreation staff members   Perform other special projects: Tabling Support, Group Fitness Support, Tennis Court Support, Vehicle Support and more.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:   6-12 months of experience in a customer service environment is preferred   Must be 18 years of age or older   Ability to pass a background check   Willing to become CPR/AED Certified (current certification preferred but will be provided)   Basic computer proficiency   Position Type Temporary Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. This job is for a current or anticipated job vacancy. Pay Rate: $17.50 - $20.00"
