    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Open-Rank-Clinical-Professor--Department-of-Medical-Sciences_R143018": {
      "title": "Open Rank Clinical Professor, Department of Medical Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About Northeastern Founded in 1898, Northeastern is a global research university and the recognized leader in experience-driven lifelong learning. Our world-renowned experiential approach empowers our students, faculty, alumni, and partners to create impact far beyond the confines of discipline, degree, and campus. Our locations—in Boston; Arlington, Charlotte, North Carolina; London; Portland, Maine; Oakland; San Francisco; Seattle; Silicon Valley; Toronto; Vancouver; and the Massachusetts communities of Burlington and Nahant—are nodes in our growing global university system. Through this network, we expand opportunities for flexible, student-centered learning and collaborative, solutions-focused research. Northeastern’s comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate programs— in a variety of on-campus and online formats—lead to degrees through the doctorate in nine colleges and schools. Among these, we offer more than 195 multi-discipline majors and degrees designed to prepare students for purposeful lives and careers. The Bouvé College of Health Sciences has over 200 faculty members, with approximately 2,000 undergraduate and 2,400 graduate students. It is the leading national model for education and research in the health, psychosocial and biomedical sciences and supports the University’s mission of educating students for a life of fulfillment and accomplishment and creating and translating knowledge to meet global and societal needs. The Department of Medical Sciences at Northeastern University is dedicated to educating and inspiring interdisciplinary professionals in medical science. We offer a range of programs, including a Doctor of Medical Science (DMSc) in Healthcare Leadership, a Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS), dual master's degree programs, and a Graduate Certificate in Extreme Medicine. Our faculty consists of experienced clinicians, researchers, and healthcare leaders. Graduates of our programs are highly sought after, with career opportunities in clinical practice, research, administration, education, and leadership roles. We are committed to shaping the future of medical science through exceptional education and innovation. About the Opportunity The Open Rank Clinical Faculty in the Doctor of Medical Sciences Healthcare is a full-time, non-tenure track position focused primarily on teaching.  The Open Rank Clinical Faculty is responsible for teaching courses within the DMSc curriculum, supporting the development and assessment of the curriculum, ensuring high-quality educational delivery, and providing student advising and mentorship.  The position also carries expectations for scholarship, including contributions to the advancement of healthcare leadership and health professions education, as well as service to the program, university, and broader professional community.  The Open Rank Clinical Faculty will participate in any additional activities necessary to maintain Northeastern at the forefront of healthcare leadership education.  Rank determined by experience and qualifications.  The position is primarily remote with some on-ground requirements. About the Opportunity Teaching Teach courses in healthcare leadership, management, policy, and related areas, providing high-quality instruction and fostering an engaging learning environment. Develop and update course materials, syllabi, and assessments aligned with current trends and best practices in healthcare leadership. Advise and mentor students, offering guidance on academic and career paths in healthcare leadership. Contribute to the development and enhancement of the program curriculum, incorporating emerging trends, technologies, and challenges in the healthcare industry. Oversee and guide students in their thesis research projects, ensuring adherence to ethical guidelines and research protocols. Support students in formulating research questions, designing studies, and analyzing data relevant to healthcare leadership. Provide regular feedback and support throughout the thesis research process, including critical evaluation of methodology, data interpretation, and scholarly writing. Create an inclusive and supportive research environment, fostering students' independent thinking, creativity, and professionalism. Facilitate opportunities for students to present their research findings, both within the program and at external conferences or symposiums. Service Participate in institutional service, actively contributing to academic policies, program development, and strategic planning. Foster collaborations and interdisciplinary partnerships within the department and across disciplines to promote innovative research and educational initiatives. Serve on appropriate Program, Department, School, College and University committees as determined by workload. Engage in outreach activities, such as serving on advisory boards, partnering with healthcare organizations, or participating in community events, to contribute to the healthcare leadership community. Actively recruit and mentor prospective applicants and participate in the admissions process. Research and Scholarship Conduct research and scholarly activities related to healthcare leadership and management. Publish research findings in reputable journals and present at conferences and professional events. Maintain an active presence in professional organizations and networks, staying up to date with industry developments and advancements. Qualifications Ph.D., Ed.D., DMSc, DHS, or equivalent doctoral degree in a Healthcare Related Field by the appointment start date. Demonstrated expertise in healthcare leadership and management, supported by a strong publication record and research accomplishments. A minimum of (5) five years of experience in healthcare or clinical research. A minimum of (3) three years of education experience (i.e. lecturer, preceptor, or as a core faculty member) Prior experience in teaching and mentoring students in healthcare leadership or administration. Proficiency with computer technology (i.e. Microsoft Office suite, word processing, e-mail, spreadsheets, databases) Ability to engage students in active learning and foster critical thinking skills. Strong research skills, including the ability to design and conduct studies, analyze data, and disseminate research findings. Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, with the ability to effectively communicate complex concepts to diverse audiences. Commitment to ongoing professional development and staying current with advancements in healthcare leadership practices and policies. Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines. Collaborative mindset and the ability to work effectively within a team environment. Interested candidates should apply here with a curriculum vitae that includes a list of publications, statements addressing the prompts below, and the names and contacts of at least three references. Successful faculty at Northeastern will be dynamic and innovative scholars with a record of research and teaching excellence and a commitment to contributing to improved equity, diversity, and inclusion. Thus, strong candidates for this faculty position will have the experiences, knowledge, and skills to build their research, pedagogy, and curriculum in ways that reflect and enhance this commitment. Please indicate how your experience, knowledge, and skills have prepared you to contribute to this work with written statements addressing the following prompts: Teaching statement (2 page maximum): Please summarize your past instructional and mentorship experiences, your pedagogical philosophy, your plans/goals for teaching in the Bouvé College of Health Sciences (including existing and proposed courses), and your strategies for teaching and mentoring global student populations.   All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by the law. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: 52-week Salary Ranges: Assistant Clinical Professor: $116,000.00 - $131,000.00 | Associate Clinical Professor: $121,000.00 - $154,000.00 | Clinical Professor: $154,000.00 - $174,000.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Director-of-Enrollment-Analytics_R143023": {
      "title": "Director of Enrollment Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Enrollment Analytics, the Director of Enrollment Analytics ensures that the division runs effectively and provides accurate and efficient delivery of required reports. The Director is responsible for developing and enhancing the undergraduate enrollment forecasting model and federal aid forecasting. The Director drives ongoing process improvement and represents the department in meetings to share and explain findings. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Reporting and Tableau Environment Delegate work related to and maintain the Tableau reporting environment, which draws from all Enrollment Management source databases Develop and maintain reports and dashboards in a Tableau Server environment covering all aspects of enrollment management, from student recruitment and admissions through student persistence and graduation Manage Tableau Server access to support data security and provide consultation and support to end users Solicit and incorporate feedback on potential enhancements Oversee the reporting environment’s structure to ensure organization and consistency across reports Maintain and track Enrollment Management goals Data Standards and Quality Monitor data standards and consistency within the Undergraduate Admission application system Ensure the successful transfer of data to the Operational Data Store and data warehouse Facilitate the resolution of data discrepancies and data-quality issues Provide authoritative data to ensure consistent results across Enrollment Management units Collaborate with University Decision Support Research to produce data in accordance with compliance standards for internal and external reporting Represent Enrollment Management as an admissions data subject matter expert on university-wide workgroups and committees related to data standards Ad Hoc Reporting Work directly with individuals across Enrollment Management and other university units on ad hoc reports and presentations requiring quantitative input Present recruitment and enrollment data as a member of the Yield Strategies and Enrollment Aid Strategies teams Staff Management and Supervision Oversee data analysts focused on undergraduate enrollment analytics and ensure the team has appropriate coverage across all subject areas Provide consistent feedback to help team members develop in their roles and achieve their professional goals Plan and organize resources, assign and delegate activities, and measure results to meet organizational expectations Enrollment Forecasting and Data Science Develop and continually enhance models for predicting learner behavior, including yield forecasting, affinity modeling, enrollment patterns, and revenue forecasting Systems and Technology Collaborate with the Enrollment Management division’s Business Intelligence team and other key departments to identify business requirements for technological enhancements and address analytical system and database needs and issues Promotion of Data Literacy Engage stakeholders to ensure users are aware of available offerings, understand how to read and interpret reports and dashboards, and receive offerings that meet their needs Minimum Qualifications Required Knowledge and skills typically acquired through completion of a Bachelor’s degree in a quantitative field At least five to seven years of demonstrated experience in a data analyst or reporting role Advanced practical experience with data management, reporting analysis, and data visualization software, including Tableau, Alteryx, R, Python, SPSS, and Cognos Demonstrated ability to analyze data, recognize patterns, and understand various data structures and common data extraction and transformation methods Ability to provide informed recommendations to nontechnical audiences in support of decision-making Experience managing and directing teams to ensure tasks and reports are delivered accurately and on time Excellent verbal, written, organizational, and time-management skills Ability to manage multiple concurrent projects and activities while maintaining attention to detail Preferred Master’s degree Experience in higher education Experience writing Structured Query Language (SQL) code to query databases Experience managing analytics professionals Position Type Data Planning and Analysis Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 111S Expected Hiring Range: $87,785.00 - $123,998.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Part-Time-Lecturer---School-of-Public-Policy-and-Urban-Affairs_R142997": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer - School of Public Policy and Urban Affairs",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Social Sciences and Humanities and its nine tenure units are the home of the Experiential Liberal Arts. Through its research, teaching, and engagement missions, the college collaborates across the university, the Northeastern network, and partners around the globe. Responsibilities: The School of Public Policy and Urban Affairs in the College of Social Sciences and Humanities seeks applicants to teach courses for one of the degree programs within the School of Public Policy and Urban Affairs, such as, but not limited to, Urban Planning and Policy; Public Administration; Public Policy; Law and Public Policy; Urban Informatics; International Affairs; or Environmental Science and Policy. Teaching might be on-line and/or in a traditional classroom. Positions are available throughout the year contingent upon enrollment and departmental need. Qualifications: Terminal degree preferred. Advanced (masters) degree with relevant professional experience may be considered. Documents to Submit: Cover letter and CV. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,085."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Part-Time-Lecturer---Law-and-Public-Policy_R142998": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer - Law and Public Policy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Social Sciences and Humanities and its nine tenure units are the home of the Experiential Liberal Arts. Through its research, teaching, and engagement missions, the college collaborates across the university, the Northeastern network, and partners around the globe. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses for the CSSH minor in Law & Public Policy, such as, but not limited to: Introduction to Law; Introduction to Law & Public Policy; Special Topics in Law & Public Policy. Teaching will be on ground in a traditional classroom setting.  Please note teaching experience and subject matter expertise in cover letter.     Positions are available throughout the year contingent upon enrollment and departmental need.   Qualifications:  J.D. or PhD degree required. Previous teaching experience highly favored.   Documents to Submit: Cover Letter , Resume , References   Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,085."
