    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Part-Time-Lecturer---School-of-Criminology-and-Criminal-Justice_R143004": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer - School of Criminology and Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Social Sciences and Humanities and its nine tenure units are the home of the Experiential Liberal Arts. Through its research, teaching, and engagement missions, the college collaborates across the university, the Northeastern network, and partners around the globe.    Responsibilities: The School of Criminology and Criminal Justice is home to the Center on Crime, Race and Justice.  Together, the School and Center prepare students for professional and research careers in criminal justice, criminology, and related fields by applying multidisciplinary and comparative social science to understand, predict, and explain crime and contribute to the development of public policy within urban communities. Using an active learning approach, the School seeks to develop its students intellectually and ethically, while providing them with a keen appreciation for the complexities of crime, and public and private efforts to make communities safer and ensure justice. The School has a Bachelor’s Degree program, a Master’s Degree program, and a Doctoral program in Criminology and Criminal Justice Policy. Further information about the School and Center can be found online at http://www.northeastern.edu/cssh/sccj/ . Our preferred availability is for classes to take place between the hours of 8:00am and 9:00pm. Please indicate availability in the cover letter. We are especially interested in candidates with a commitment to high quality instruction at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. All qualified applications will be kept on file for additional openings. Positions are available throughout the year contingent upon enrollment and departmental need. Qualifications: Master’s Degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or related social science discipline is required. A JD is required for all law courses. Preference will be given to individuals with teaching ability in the areas of Criminal Law, Security, Policing, Violence, Victimology, and Research Methods, and Forensic Science. Documents to Submit: CV and Cover Letter required. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,085."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Oakland-CA/Adjunct-Faculty---School-of-Criminology-and-Criminal-Justice---Oakland--CA_R143007": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – School of Criminology and Criminal Justice – Oakland, CA",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Social Sciences and Humanities and its nine tenure units are the home of the Experiential Liberal Arts. Through its research, teaching, and engagement missions, the college collaborates across the university, the Northeastern network, and partners around the globe.    Responsibilities: The School of Criminology and Criminal Justice is home to the Center on Crime, Race and Justice.  Together, the School and Center prepare students for professional and research careers in criminal justice, criminology, and related fields by applying multidisciplinary and comparative social science to understand, predict, and explain crime and contribute to the development of public policy within urban communities. Using an active learning approach, the School seeks to develop its students intellectually and ethically, while providing them with a keen appreciation for the complexities of crime, and public and private efforts to make communities safer and ensure justice. The School has a Bachelor’s Degree program, a Master’s Degree program, and a Doctoral program in Criminology and Criminal Justice Policy. Further information about the School and Center can be found online at http://www.northeastern.edu/cssh/sccj/ . Our preferred availability is for classes to take place between the hours of 8:00am and 9:00pm. Please indicate availability in the cover letter. We are especially interested in candidates with a commitment to high quality instruction at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. All qualified applications will be kept on file for additional openings. Positions are available throughout the year contingent upon enrollment and departmental need. Qualifications: Master’s Degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or related social science discipline is required. A JD is required for all law courses. Preference will be given to individuals with teaching ability in the areas of Criminal Law, Security, Policing, Violence, Victimology, and Research Methods, and Forensic Science. Documents to Submit: CV and Cover Letter required. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,484.48."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Arlington-VA/Part-Time-Lecturer---School-of-Criminology-and-Criminal-Justice---Arlington--VA_R143006": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer - School of Criminology and Criminal Justice - Arlington, VA",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Social Sciences and Humanities and its nine tenure units are the home of the Experiential Liberal Arts. Through its research, teaching, and engagement missions, the college collaborates across the university, the Northeastern network, and partners around the globe.    Responsibilities: The School of Criminology and Criminal Justice in the College of Social Sciences and Humanities seeks applicants to teach graduate courses in the Master of Science in Criminology and Criminal Justice (MSCJ) Program at its Arlington, Virginia (National Capital/Washington, DC area) campus. Part-time instructors are needed to teach graduate courses in Criminology, Global Criminology, and Criminal Justice. Instructors are also needed to teach in topical areas, including Immigration and Crime, Security, Research Methods, and/or Statistical Analysis. Instructors will support the highly ranked MSCJ Program launching in Arlington. On a rolling basis, we will also consider candidates with qualifications to teach Research Methods and/or Statistical Analysis during the Spring 2027 semester and beyond. These courses support the Master of Criminology and Criminal Justice, Master of Public Policy, Master of Public Administration, Master of Science in Urban Informatics, and Master of Science in Applied Quantitative Methods for Social Analysis programs.  Teaching will be in a traditional classroom on our Arlington, Virginia campus with the potential to teach additional classes online for learners throughout our Global Campus Network.    Positions are available throughout the year contingent upon enrollment, funding, and programmatic needs. Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or related disciplines is preferred. Advanced (masters) degree with relevant professional experience may be considered. College-level teaching experience is preferred. Documents to Submit: Applicants should submit a cover letter and CV. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,085."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Senior-Project-Manager--DIBI_R142971-1": {
      "title": "Senior Project Manager, DIBI",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary The Defense Industrial Base Institute is looking for a skilled Senior Project Manager to join its execution team of researchers, students, staff, and faculty. The Senior Project Manager will advise, consult, and guide the project management process for multiple large-scale, complex, cross-organizational projects within a research portfolio funded by federal agencies such as the Navy, Air Force, and National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA). The Senior Project Manager will work closely with each project’s stakeholders to define project charters and schedules and ensure compliance with budgets (or amendments). This role oversees the entire project lifecycle to deliver comprehensive solutions that are well thought out, innovative, and repeatable, while excelling in scope, time, and budget management. The Senior Project Manager adapts, reacts, and adjusts quickly to changing conditions, identifies risks, and recommends solutions. Responsibilities are broad in scope and encompass a wide variety of activities that require rapid shifts in priorities. This position is a one-year appointment tied to federal funding. US citizenship is a requirement of the federal sponsor. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities 1. Project Management (50%) Lead the definition of project scope and objectives, involving all relevant stakeholders and ensuring technical feasibility Organize complex projects into structured phases and sprints to prioritize speed, improvements, and enhancements Create and maintain comprehensive project documentation, including the project charter, communication plan, Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Informed (RACI) matrix, risk register, and process maps to document needs Develop detailed, comprehensive project plans to monitor and track progress Manage changes to project scope, schedule, and costs using appropriate verification techniques Assist Principal Investigators (PIs), Co-Principal Investigators (Co-PIs), and project teams in analyzing progress, making decisions, prioritizing, and assessing and mitigating risk Perform risk management to minimize project risks Manage relationships with clients and all stakeholders Meet with clients to take detailed ordering briefs and clarify the specific requirements of each project Coordinate internal resources and third parties/vendors for the flawless execution of projects, ensuring resource availability and allocation Delegate project tasks Measure and track project performance using appropriate tools and techniques, specifically to analyze the successful completion of short- and long-term goals Report and escalate to management as needed 2. Project Management Service Development (25%) Contribute to ongoing service development, including the design, development, and maintenance of a library of standardized project management templates Lead efforts to identify new applications of project management principles, drive adoption of these practices and templates, and mature these capabilities Assist with the development of an internal project status dashboard Serve as a mentor to others and may act as a resource for staff assigned to informally lead projects on behalf of their respective departments 3. Leadership Select, onboard, and continually develop employees in a way that creates an environment that inspires them to do their best work Set clear goals and expectations and delegate work effectively Provide timely feedback about performance throughout the year before conducting a final performance review Minimum Qualifications Knowledge and skills normally acquired through completion of a Bachelor’s degree and a minimum of 5–7 years of experience leading complex projects Experience working in a defense, market agency, or government environment Advanced knowledge of a variety of project management concepts, methodologies, practices, and procedures Project Management Professional (PMP), knowledge of Agile Scrum practices, program management, and Six Sigma Green Belt or Black Belt Expertise in Salesforce.gov, Smartsheet.gov, or similar project management tools Strong planning skills applied through relevant software Excellent written, verbal, client-facing, and internal communication skills Solid organizational skills, including attention to detail and multitasking US citizenship required by federal sponsor Ability to travel up to 30% of the time Required Documents Resume Position Type General Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 111S Expected Hiring Range: $87,785.00 - $123,998.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Business-Operations-Admin-Assistant_R143016": {
      "title": "Business Operations Admin Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary: We are seeking a Business Operations Administrative Assistant to provide essential administrative, operational, and personnel support for the Makerspace at EXP and Wetlab Makerspace, working independently and reporting directly to the Executive Director - Makerspace. This role is responsible for maintaining organized records and compliance documentation, managing day-to-day projects, supporting personnel functions such as onboarding and recruiting, coordinating schedules, and handling purchasing needs. The ideal candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable managing a variety of responsibilities with minimal oversight in a dynamic, hands-on environment. Minimum Qualifications: Prior experience in administrative, operations, or office management roles preferred Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to prioritize competing demands Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment Familiarity with purchasing processes a plus (Workday purchasing) Proficiency with standard office software (e.g., Microsoft Office/Google Workspace) Key Responsibilities : Administrative Management (50%) Maintain accurate and organized records across administrative, operational, and programmatic functions Prepare, track, and maintain compliance documentation to ensure adherence to organizational and regulatory requirements Monitor and respond to email correspondence in a timely and professional manner, routing inquiries as needed Personnel Management (20%) Coordinate and manage the onboarding process for new student staff and/or makerspace patrons Support recruiting efforts, including posting openings, screening candidates, and coordinating interviews Coordinate scheduling for staff, meetings, and events, ensuring efficient use of time and resources Purchasing (20%) Manage purchasing processes, including ordering supplies, equipment, and materials Track expenditures, maintain vendor relationships, and ensure purchases align with budget guidelines Other duties as assigned (10%) Support the Executive Director and broader team with additional administrative or operational tasks as needed Position Type Temporary Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. This job is for a current or anticipated job vacancy. Pay Rate:"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Part-Time-Lecturer---Theater_R142898-2": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer - Theater",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Arts, Media and Design is looking for Part Time Lecturers to teach undergraduate courses in the Department of Theatre in the upcoming 2026-2027 Academic year. Applicants will be reviewed on a rolling basis and courses will start in September 2026. Qualifications: Ph.D., M.F.A. or Master’s Degree and extensive professional experience required; previous teaching on the college level is preferred. Individuals with experience teaching courses related to Fashion and Improv are encouraged to apply. Additional Job Description Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit starts at $2,085 per credit hour."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Portland-ME/Contracts-and-Budget-Manager-Rural-Health-Transformation-Program--RHTP-_R143063": {
      "title": "Contracts and Budget Manager-Rural Health Transformation Program (RHTP)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The Roux Institute at Northeastern University serves as a Consolidated Partner to the Maine Department of Health and Human Services on Initiative 5 (Sustainable Rural Health Ecosystems) of Maine's Rural Health Transformation Program (RHTP). As part of this role, the Roux Institute is responsible for identifying, subcontracting with, and managing a portfolio of Contracted Vendors, administering pass-through funds, and managing Department-approved Hospital Efficiency Funds distributed to a cohort of Maine rural hospitals. The Contracts and Budget Manager will provide day-to-day contracting and financial administration support across this initiative, working closely with the Northeastern University Office of General Counsel (OGC) and NU finance teams to support execution of sub-award agreements, consultant and vendor contracts, and hospital efficiency fund agreements, and tracking associated compliance and invoicing requirements. This role serves as an important operational link between Roux program leadership, University central offices, and external Contracted Vendors and hospital partners, helping to ensure that contracting and payment processes move efficiently and in compliance with University policy and Department requirements, and State and Federal (CMS) requirements in a complex environment. This position requires strong financial capabilities, organizational skills, comfort working with contracts, spreadsheets and government documentation, and the ability to track multiple agreements and deadlines simultaneously across a fast-moving, high-visibility state initiative. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree required, preferably in business administration, public administration, finance, or a related field, and 4-6 years of relevant experience in contract administration, grants/financial administration, or a similar operations role. Experience supporting contract or sub-award processes (e.g., drafting/routing agreements, tracking approvals, coordinating with legal/finance offices) or previous roles in grant administration strongly preferred. Knowledge of sub-award agreements, consultant contracts, invoicing, and basic compliance requirements (e.g., insurance certificates, W-9s, scopes of work); experience in a university, government, or grant-funded environment is a plus. Strong attention to detail and comfort managing sensitive financial and contractual information with discretion. Excellent organizational and time-management skills; ability to track a high volume of agreements, deliverables, and deadlines across multiple vendors and hospitals. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to liaise professionally and effectively with University offices (Office of General Counsel, finance/accounts payable) and external vendors/hospital administrators. Proficiency with Excel and other Microsoft Office Suite products and University financial/procurement systems (e.g., Workday or equivalent); willingness to learn new systems as needed. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and escalate issues appropriately when navigating University policy or compliance questions. Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Building-Safety-Manager-2_R143065": {
      "title": "Building Safety Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity JOB SUMMARY The Building Safety Manager (BSM) serves as an embedded lab safety professional who provides environmental health and safety guidance, oversight, and support for research and teaching laboratories within their assigned buildings on the Northeastern Boston campus. The BSM advises Principal Investigators, lab personnel, Department Safety Officers (DSOs), and College Safety Officers (CSOs) on safe laboratory practices and regulatory compliance across chemical, biological, and radiation safety. Through regular building walkthroughs, lab inspections, and ongoing relationship-building with research groups, the BSM identifies hazards, recommends corrective actions, and helps labs understand and meet applicable city, state, and federal safety regulations. This can include supporting the appropriate management of hazardous material inventories within defined control areas, in coordination with lab personnel and Facilities. The BSM is a key point of contact for their local research community. The BSM also participates in building-level emergency planning, incident response, and coordinates with Northeastern's ECOS (Environmental Compliance and Occupational Safety) team on hazardous waste handling when needed. The role requires strong interpersonal skills, sound judgment to build trust with research groups, the ability to communicate risk clearly, and promote a collaborative, non-punitive safety culture rather than a purely enforcement-driven one. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in a physical science, life science, environmental science, engineering, occupational safety, or other applicable area Minimum of five years demonstrated work experience in meeting EHS requirements in a laboratory setting Preferred Qualifications Employment experience within higher education Experience in hazardous material emergency planning Experience in laboratory process safety Master’s degree in one of the fields listed above Background in laboratory research and environmental health and safety compliance in research laboratories Necessary Skills: Working knowledge of the regulatory landscape governing laboratory operations (OSHA, RCRA, Massachusetts DEP, NFPA, and related standards), with the ability to translate regulatory requirements into practical, actionable guidance for lab personnel Experience conducting laboratory inspections, hazard and risk assessments, and tracking corrective actions to closure Ability to effectively negotiate and influence the safety behavior of PIs and research, building credibility and trust Experience fostering a collaborative, non-punitive safety culture across research groups with varying levels of safety maturity Experience with laboratory safety data management and tracking platforms Ability to coordinate across multiple internal stakeholders such as Facilities, Department and College Safety Officers, ECOS, and other OARS programs on cross-functional safety initiatives Experience responding to and participating in investigation of laboratory incidents and emergencies, including coordination with emergency responders Ability to assist with hazardous material emergencies and post-event remediation Ability to operate instrumentation used to monitor personnel chemical exposures and evaluate monitoring results Excellent time, organizational, and project management skills, including planning, prioritizing, and scheduling multiple ongoing projects to work independently and with the BSM team Demonstrated ability to work with a diverse population and foster a collaborative work environment Be medically qualified to wear respiratory protection and other personal protective equipment Lift up to 50 lbs and move up to 500 lbs of materials using rolling carts or drum carts. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACCOUNTABILITIES 1) Laboratory Safety Support and Inspections Serve as the primary safety advisor for PIs, lab managers, and research staff within assigned buildings. Conduct regular lab inspections and building walkthroughs to identify hazards and unsafe practices.  Work collaboratively with lab personnel to develop corrective action plans. Support labs through the General Lab Inspection Program and related OARS inspection workflows, including documentation of findings and follow-up. Advise on risk assessments, hazard analysis, and appropriate PPE use. Support lab design projects related to lab safety. Build and maintain working relationships with DSOs, CSOs, College Directors, and PIs to ensure safety concerns are understood and addressed collaboratively. 2) Hazardous Material and Waste Coordination Support labs in understanding and maintaining compliance with Maximum Available Quantities (MAQs) storage thresholds within defined control areas, partnering with lab personnel and Facilities to flag and resolve potential issues as they arise. Coordinate with Northeastern's ECOS team on hazardous waste handoffs and routing. 3) Building-Wide Emergency Planning and Response Participate in the development and maintenance of Emergency Action Plans (EAPs) for assigned buildings, in collaboration with other Northeastern safety professionals such as Emergency Management, lab supervisors and other stakeholders. Maintain awareness of building-wide hazards, equipment, and ongoing research activities to support emergency responders during incidents. Participate in a rotating on-call emergency response team, incident investigations, and help identify and implement corrective actions.   4) Program Development, Support, and Continuity Contribute to the development of OARS projects and programs, including writing guidance, leading working groups, and more, as directed. Maintain up-to-date documentation of building assignments, in-progress work, and key contacts to support team continuity. Participate in OARS programs as they relate to assigned buildings, supporting college and lab-level engagement. Assist with start-up and decommissioning of laboratory operations. Serve as a source of regulatory information for lab personnel and perform other technical or administrative duties as directed. Pursue ongoing professional development through conferences, training, and certifications. Position Type Legal and Regulatory Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 110S Expected Hiring Range: $76,335.00 - $107,823.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Oakland-CA/Adjunct-Faculty---English---Oakland_R140958-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - English - Oakland",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Social Sciences and Humanities  and its nine tenure units are the home of the Experiential Liberal Arts. Through its research, teaching, and engagement missions, the college collaborates across the university, the Northeastern network, and partners around the globe.  We are strongly committed to fostering excellence through diversity and enthusiastically welcome nominations and applications from members of groups underrepresented in academia. Successful faculty in the College of Social Sciences and Humanities will be dynamic and innovative scholars with a record of research and teaching excellence and a commitment to improved equity, diversity, and inclusion. Strong candidates for this position will have the expertise, knowledge, and skills to build their research, pedagogy, and curriculum in ways that reflect and enhance this commitment.   Responsibilities: The Department of English in the College of Social Sciences and Humanities seeks applications for part-time writing instructors on the Oakland Campus. Adjunct faculty are to teach required writing courses that include First-Year Writing, as well as a variety of Advanced Writing courses that focus on disciplinary writing practices, including specialized courses in technical writing, business writing, writing for the health professions, and interdisciplinary writing. First-Year and Advanced Writing courses are also available in sections for multilingual writers. For a general introduction to the Writing Programs, please see http://www.northeastern.edu/cssh/english/writing-program/ .   Positions available throughout the year contingent upon enrollment and department need. Qualifications: M.A. in English or equivalent required.   Documents to Submit: Cover letter and CV. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa.  The rate per credit is $2,435.76         Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,435.76."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Assistant-Project-Manager_R143092": {
      "title": "Assistant Project Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity JOB SUMMARY The Assistant Project Manager (APM) will have a broad set of skills within the realm of project delivery from planning through project completion. The APM will be involved in any or all typical project phases including Pre-Design, Design, Construction, and Project Closeout.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree plus two years of experience in construction, project management, engineering, or architecture; or eight years of equivalent experience in lieu of a degree. Ability to read and interpret project reports, construction drawings, specifications, and internal and external communications. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Microsoft Project, Trimble Unity Construct (TUC), and Procore. Ability to work independently on complex tasks and make sound decisions. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to prioritize workload, anticipate project needs, and manage meetings and supporting documentation (agendas, minutes, action items). Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain concepts clearly and build effective working relationships. Strong problem-solving skills.   KEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACCOUNTABILITIES Project Planning & Coordination Assist in developing project schedules, timelines, and work plans Help create and maintain project budgets and cost estimates Coordinate with architects, engineers, and design teams on project specifications Support the development of project execution plans Documentation & Administration Update and maintain project information in spreadsheets and TUC.  Manage submittals, RFIs (Requests for Information), and change orders Maintain project files, contracts, and correspondence Prepare and distribute meeting minutes Track project documentation for compliance and record-keeping On-Site Coordination Conduct or support site visits and progress inspections Communicate with site superintendents and Northeastern Clerks of the Works Coordination of installations or furniture and other 'soft cost' items within projects. Help resolve on-site issues and coordinate problem-solving Monitor quality control and safety compliance Financial Tracking Assist with budget tracking and cost reporting Review and process invoices and payment applications Help track change orders and their budget impact Support forecasting of project costs to completion Communication & Stakeholder Management Prepare progress reports and status updates Attend owner/architect/contractor (OAC) meetings Help manage client expectations and address concerns Coordination with in-house trades departments (Carpentry Shop, Transportation, Sign Shop, etc.). Scheduling Support Update and maintain project schedules Track milestones and flag potential delays Risk & Compliance Management Help identify potential project risks and mitigation strategies Ensure compliance with building codes, safety regulations, and contract terms Support quality assurance/quality control (QA/QC) processes   Position Type Facilities Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Cabot-Building-Supervisor--Temporary-_R143026": {
      "title": "Cabot Building Supervisor (Temporary)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary: The Building Supervisor is responsible for maintaining a safe, secure, and welcoming environment for students, employees, and visitors. This position oversees front-desk access control, monitors building entry and exit, conducts routine security checks, and supervises student employees assigned to front-desk duties. The Building Supervisor serves as a visible point of contact at the building’s front desk and ensures that established building access and security procedures are consistently followed.   Essential Responsibilities: Monitor and manage access to the building through the front desk. Verify identification, authorization, or other credentials as required before permitting access. Maintain awareness of individuals entering and exiting the building. Provide a professional and helpful first point of contact for students, employees, visitors, and guests. Maintain accurate access, incident, and other required logs. Respond appropriately to questions, concerns, and unusual or unauthorized access attempts. Follow established procedures for after-hours access and restricted areas. Conduct routine walkthroughs of the building to ensure doors, entrances, and other designated access points are properly secured. Check that exterior and designated interior doors are locked and functioning properly. Identify and report security concerns, damaged locks, doors, alarms, lighting, or other facility issues. Monitor for unusual activity and promptly escalate security or safety concerns to the appropriate emergency personnel. Ensure front-desk and security operations remain adequately staffed during assigned hours. Perform other related duties as assigned.   Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent required; additional experience in security, facilities management, or a related field preferred. Previous experience in building operations, security, front-desk services, customer service, or a related role preferred. Ability to follow established building access, security, and emergency response procedures. Strong observational skills and the ability to recognize, assess, and report unusual activity or potential safety and security concerns. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact professionally and respectfully with students, employees, visitors, and guests. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and handle sensitive situations with discretion and professionalism. Ability to maintain accurate records, logs, and incident reports. Ability to supervise, guide, and provide direction to student employees and ensure front-desk responsibilities are carried out appropriately. Basic computer skills and the ability to learn and use access control systems, communication tools, and other relevant technology. Ability to conduct routine building walkthroughs and check doors, entrances, and other designated access points. Ability to work assigned shifts, including evenings, weekends, or holidays, as required by operational needs. Commitment to maintaining a safe, secure, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all building occupants and visitors.   Work Schedule: Expected work hours are between 8:00 p.m. and 12:30 a.m. Weekend shifts may vary based on building operational needs and staffing requirements. Flexibility to work evening and weekend hours is required.   Position Type Temporary Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. This job is for a current or anticipated job vacancy. Pay Rate:"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Site-Reliability-Engineer_R143033": {
      "title": "Site Reliability Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About Khoury College Khoury College is committed to building a community of belonging among students, faculty and staff. We strongly encourage applicants from individuals with disabilities, veterans, and those with varied experiences and backgrounds. We invite you to join a fast-moving, ambitious college with an underlying mission that is driven by our motto of “CS for Everyone.” About the National Deep Inference Fabric The National Deep Inference Fabric (NDIF) is an artificial intelligence (AI) research infrastructure project funded by $9 million from the National Science Foundation (NSF) and more than $4 million from private foundations. Its mission is to create an innovative, highly transparent, large-scale AI inference infrastructure that enables cutting-edge scientific research on the largest open AI models. Job Summary NDIF is seeking an experienced Site Reliability Engineer to advance the reliability and coordinate the day-to-day operations of its growing research platform. This role creates systems that keep distributed services healthy and available, makes clusters easier to debug and operate, and builds tooling that enables the platform to scale as demand and deployments grow. This is a hands-on role with significant latitude for assessing complex technical problems, determining priorities, and delivering innovations with minimal oversight. A research background is not required, but knowledge of machine learning operations (MLOps) is highly desirable. The successful candidate will have experience operating production systems, a commitment to operating them well, and motivation to contribute to AI safety and interpretability. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Measure and improve the reliability, availability, and performance of the platform used by research teams Build and maintain observability systems so issues are detected early and debugging is proactive rather than reactive Improve operational tooling and automation, including continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD), automated testing, and infrastructure as code Create effective workflows for debugging and resolving issues across the distributed stack, including Ray connectivity, graphics processing unit (GPU) and resource allocation, and scheduling Partner with the broader NDIF team to keep the system dependable and usable as user needs evolve Establish and advocate for operational best practices as the platform grows Minimum Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree in computer science, engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience At least 3 years of experience or more in site reliability engineering (SRE) or a closely related role Experience operating distributed systems in production, with a track record of owning complex systems end to end Strong Python skills and comfort working with backend services Experience with observability tooling such as Prometheus and Grafana, or equivalent tools Working command of CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, and infrastructure as code Judgment to debug and optimize systems with minimal guidance, along with communication skills that keep teams aligned Genuine interest in AI safety, interpretability, and supporting interdisciplinary research Preferred Knowledge of MLOps Required Documents Resume Position Type Information Technology Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 111S Expected Hiring Range: $87,785.00 - $123,998.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant_R143056": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary The Main Office Administrative Assistant serves as the primary point of contact for the Department of Mathematics, providing front desk coverage, community services, event coordination, and administrative support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. The role requires a consistently positive and professional demeanor, strong attention to detail, flexibility, and the ability to manage shifting priorities in a fast-paced environment. Initiative is a priority, including the ability to identify what needs to be done and act independently without needing to be explicitly asked. Strong communication, tact, organizational and computer skills, and a genuine willingness to pitch in and support the department are essential. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Front Desk & Community Services Provide consistent front desk coverage, ensuring the reception area projects a professional and welcoming environment; answer the telephone and respond to emails in a timely manner Support students, faculty, staff, and visitors and monitor front desk traffic Maintain a neat and orderly work environment Apply advanced understanding of department programs, policies, and university resources to resolve routine and non-routine inquiries Serve as departmental liaison to Information Technology Services (ITS), Facilities, the copying center, and other university offices Purchasing & Budget Monitoring Purchase and monitor department supplies as needed Maintain detailed Excel purchase records and retain receipts in a shared folder Liaise with student clubs to support their activities and coordinate catering needs Monitor spending across all department purchases and student club budgets Room Management & Facilities Manage room scheduling, ensure functioning audiovisual (A/V) equipment, and arrange seminar room cleaning when required Submit work orders and liaise with Facilities to ensure the department is clean, safe, and fully functioning Maintain office equipment Assist with assigning offices to faculty, graduate students, and visitors Records & Correspondence Maintain organized electronic filing and records management systems Manage department mail, package deliveries, and inter-office correspondence Manage department listservs and email distribution lists and disseminate departmental communications Event Coordination Plan, organize, and coordinate department events, including faculty speaker seminars and other student- and research-facing initiatives Manage event logistics from start to finish, including space reservations, catering, A/V, signage, materials, attendee communications, on-site setup, and post-event follow-up Prepare event materials, briefing documents, and printed programs; manage the department event calendar and flag scheduling conflicts Coordinate travel and hospitality for visiting speakers and faculty candidates and process reimbursements with the Budget Coordinator General Assist with additional projects and administrative tasks as needed Minimum Qualifications Required Associate's degree Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, and Teams Consistently positive attitude and professional demeanor with strong attention to detail Ability to work in a fast-paced environment, manage competing priorities, and remain flexible as priorities shift Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to interact professionally with individuals at all levels, internal and external to the department, with tact and diplomacy Readiness to take on responsibility and willingness to pitch in and help others Strong initiative, with the ability to identify what needs to be done and act independently without close supervision Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, exercise sound independent judgment, and carry out complex assignments with minimal supervision Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to draft professional correspondence, presentations, and reports on behalf of the department High level of discretion in handling confidential information Preferred Bachelor's degree Experience with university systems such as Concur or Workday Position Type General Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 106H Expected Hiring Range: $23.37 - $32.14 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/News-Reporter_R143085-1": {
      "title": "News Reporter",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Summary Northeastern Global News (NGN), Northeastern University’s award-winning, fast-paced, daily news organization is looking for a talented News Reporter to be based on Northeastern’s Boston campus.     The ideal candidate is an experienced journalist and versatile storyteller who is especially skilled at data, AI and science reporting – and can write engaging and deeply reported articles. The News Reporter should be ready to quickly jump on breaking news, providing commentary and analysis by faculty experts on timely topics that captivate national and global conversations.   NGN showcases news about innovation across Northeastern's academic and research enterprise, including but not limited to stories about discoveries, innovations across multiple fields, experiential learning, human interest stories, and campus life inside labs, classrooms, and beyond.    We expect curiosity, accountability, creativity, and a commitment to accuracy and speed.   This role is perfect for a journalist who thrives in a fast-paced environment, has great news judgment, and understands how to reach readers across digital platforms, particularly through data reporting and stories that highlight the increasing dominance of AI and its influence in transforming the workplace, health care and academia, among other sectors.   The News Reporter must have several years of experience working for daily commercial news organizations. The experience should include analyzing complicated academic studies and data and translating them into deeply reported articles that are easily understandable to a wide audience, understanding scientific methodology, adherence to factchecking, and the ability to file daily stories under tight deadlines.   NGN is part of Northeastern’s Communications team in External Affairs. Reporting to the Executive Editor of NGN, the News Reporter is part of a team of journalists who work closely with media relations, social media and multimedia teams within Communications. It is a highly data-informed organization with ambitious goals and impeccable standards.   The position is based on the Boston campus and is fully on site, five days a week. Remote or hybrid work are not an option. As is the case for every member of the Communications team, after-hours work, including weekends and holidays, is routinely required. Minimum Qualifications 5 - 7 years reporting experience with a commercial daily news organization (digital or print). Demonstrated ability to handle data, AI and science news coverage with speed and accuracy. Strong writing, interviewing, and source-building skills. Excellent news judgment. Experience interpreting public documents, filings, and data. Ability to multitask, manage deadlines, and respond quickly to developing stories. Familiarity with digital publishing tools is a plus.   Good to have: Experience with multimedia or video reporting Data journalism or basic visual storytelling skills Knowledge of SEO and audience engagement strategies            Key Responsibilities Report, write, and publish breaking news, daily stories, and enterprise features for a large audience using data  Work closely with editors to refine pitches, shape coverage, and maintain high standards of accuracy. Develop reliable sources and maintain strong relationships across the Northeastern community and relevant stakeholder groups. Produce stories that are clear, engaging, and accessible to readers. Collaborate with media relations, social media, and multimedia teams to enhance stories with data, graphics, photos, and video. Monitor analytics and audience metrics to inform reporting and follow-up coverage. Adhere to guidelines and fact-check thoroughly.     Position Type Marketing and Communications Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 110S Expected Hiring Range: $76,335.00 - $107,823.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Portland-ME/Program-Coordinator-Rural-Health-Transformation-Program--RHTP-_R143066": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator-Rural Health Transformation Program (RHTP)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The Roux Institute at Northeastern University serves as a Consolidated Partner to the Maine Department of Health and Human Services on Initiative 5 (Sustainable Rural Health Ecosystems) of Maine's Rural Health Transformation Program (RHTP), co-leading the Hospital Efficiency and Stabilization work across Activity 5.1 (Hospital Efficiency and Financial Management) and Activity 5.2 (Regional Health Ecosystems Planning and Implementation). The Program Coordinator will provide logistical, administrative, and stakeholder engagement support across two closely related lines of work: (1) the Hospital Sustainability Learning Collaborative convened under Activity 5.1, and (2) the regionalized rural health ecosystems planning process convened under Activity 5.2. This position ensures that recurring convenings, individual hospital and regional stakeholder meetings, and cross-activity communications run smoothly, are well-documented, and support the Provider's obligations to the Department under this Contract. This role will work closely with the Roux Institute's RHTP project leadership, Contracted Vendors and state RHTP personnel delivering technical assistance to rural hospitals, andand engaging regional stakeholders across the state in health system coordination. Due to the statewide, multi-stakeholder nature of this initiative, this individual will routinely coordinate across organizations and levels of seniority, and must be comfortable managing a high volume of scheduling, logistics, and documentation with strong attention to detail. Minimum Qalifications Bachelor's degree required and 3-5 years of relevant experience in program or project coordination, event/meeting logistics, or administrative support, ideally in a healthcare, public health, higher education, or government-facing setting. Demonstrated experience coordinating recurring meetings, convenings, or workshops for multiple external stakeholders, including scheduling, agenda preparation, materials distribution, and notetaking. Strong analytical and technical abilities. Ability to independently deliver high quality, organized and repeatable results. Factual, direct style of communication. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail; ability to manage multiple concurrent workstreams and deadlines across two related but distinct activity areas. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the judgment and diplomacy to interact professionally with hospital leadership, state government staff, and community stakeholders. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) and virtual meeting platforms (Zoom, Microsoft Teams); comfort with survey/data collection tools (e.g., Qualtrics) and shared file systems (SharePoint) preferred. Ability to synthesize notes and input from meetings into clear, concise summaries for internal and Department-facing reporting. Knowledge of or interest in rural health, hospital operations, or health policy is a plus, but not required. Ability to exercise discretion with sensitive or confidential information related to hospital finances and operations. Position Type General Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 107S Expected Hiring Range: $53,615.00 - $75,728.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Assistant-Director---Program-Development_R142927": {
      "title": "Assistant Director - Program Development",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary The Assistant Director, Program Development supports the Associate Dean for Graduate Education in developing a portfolio of academic programs that meet the college's goals of delivering high-quality programs with strong enrollment. This role supports the development of traditional and non-traditional educational products by college departments and academic units for rollout across Northeastern’s campuses, working to create programs and educational products that satisfy prospective student demand while leveraging current and emerging areas of faculty teaching expertise. The Assistant Director develops programs aligned with the college's enrollment and teaching goals, the college's teaching expertise and capacity, and the needs of graduates' employers. The Assistant Director works with the Dean's Office to understand the college's enrollment goals and programmatic priorities, and with Central Enrollment Management to understand enrollment trends and opportunities. This role also engages directly with employers to understand hiring needs, organizes marketing and survey data related to new program development, and partners with the Innovation Planning and Development group to explore job market and technology trends and conduct market research. The Assistant Director collaborates with the Experiential Digital Global Education group on online program development. Working closely with department chairs, graduate associate chairs, and program directors, the Assistant Director develops new master's and doctoral programs that help the college achieve its strategic goals. This includes identifying programming opportunities, connecting faculty in emerging areas, and facilitating discussions among collaborators to support curriculum development and program proposals. The Assistant Director ensures new programs comply with governance, accreditation, and licensure guidelines, and collaborates with counterparts in other colleges to develop interdisciplinary programs. The Assistant Director also works with network campuses, the Dean's Office, and Central Enrollment Management to understand priorities and opportunities for program development across the network, identifying opportunities to roll out existing programs and partnering with department chairs, graduate associate chairs, and program directors to develop them. Additionally, this role works to develop non-traditional educational products, including those involving industry partners, that support the college's enrollment goals, engaging with employers to identify areas of interest and facilitating discussions with academic leadership to develop employer-focused educational modules and badges. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Organize and understand data about enrollment trends, student program interests, and employer hiring needs across campuses Develop new master's and doctoral programs that help the college achieve these goals by working with department chairs, graduate associate chairs, and program directors Understand and develop opportunities to roll out college programs across campuses Support development of non-traditional educational products, including non-credit classes, programs, pathways, modules, and badges Support opportunities for students to take cross-college classes Support online program development and online program offerings in coordination with Experiential Digital Global Education Assist Associate Director of Graduate Education in all program development activities, communication, and coordination Ensure governance, accreditation, and licensure compliance Minimum Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree (or equivalent) Minimum of 3–5 years of experience with academic and administrative projects, preferably in higher education and with adult learners or in a high customer service environment Strong project management and organizational skills with attention to detail and a commitment to quality, including the ability to consistently produce high-quality work under tight deadlines Effective interpersonal, oral presentation, and written communication skills Strong analytical skills, including the ability to interpret market research, enrollment data, and trends to inform program development decisions Ability to balance multiple demands from demanding constituencies and navigate ambiguity to drive projects forward independently Ability to function effectively as a member of a team in a dynamic, fast-paced work environment, with flexibility and initiative to navigate shifting priorities Ability to work across the organization with a wide spectrum of individuals that includes students, faculty, academic managers, program office personnel, and Deans Responsive to feedback and committed to continuous improvement Preferred Master's degree Experience with academic coordination Familiarity with academic governance, accreditation, and program approval processes Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Position Type Academic Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 108S Expected Hiring Range: $60,315.00 - $85,192.50 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Part-Time-Lecturer---Department-of-Civil-and-Environmental-Engineering--Boston-_R142870": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer - Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering (Boston)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Position Summary: The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering seeks part-time faculty to teach selected undergraduate or graduate courses within the department and its degree programs. Course topics may span a full spectrum of disciplinary or interdisciplinary areas, including opportunities to support the experiential and practice-based components increasingly integrated into undergraduate and graduate curricula. Part-time faculty play a valuable role in bringing applied, industry-informed perspective into the classroom, complementing full-time faculty capacity and helping bridge academic research with professional practice. Responsibilities: Prepare and deliver lectures, course materials, and examinations for assigned courses Design or support experiential learning components where applicable, such as project-based assignments, applied problem-solving, case studies, or industry-connected coursework Interact regularly with students, including responding to questions and providing guidance outside of scheduled class time Evaluate student performance and provide timely, substantive feedback Coordinate with department faculty and staff to ensure course content aligns with program learning outcomes and curriculum requirements Qualifications: M.S. or Ph.D. in a relevant engineering discipline (required) Professional and/or teaching experience preferred, particularly experience applying technical knowledge in professional practice settings Strong, effective verbal communication skills to engage students and explain technical material clearly Ability to bring applied, real-world perspective into instruction, especially where courses include an experiential or practice-oriented component Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,693.75"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Business-and-Entrepreneurship-Librarian_R142948": {
      "title": "Business and Entrepreneurship Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Reporting the Library Program Manager for Entrepreneurship, the Business and Entrepreneurship Librarian serves as the liaison to the D’Amore-McKim School of Business and helps coordinate the library’s interdisciplinary efforts to integrate services and resources into all entrepreneurship initiatives across campus. The Business and Entrepreneurship Librarian provides teaching, learning, and research support through virtual and in-person instructional sessions, consultations, and workshops.   Additionally, the Business and Entrepreneurship Librarian will collaborate to support business & entrepreneurship initiatives in Boston and across the global campus network. The successful candidate is: Inclined to investigate artificial intelligence tools to gain an understanding of how they affect the learning environment Eager to apply an entrepreneurial mindset to their work; experiment, learn, adapt, and iterate Thrive in a fast-paced environment If you have any questions or you would like to chat about the position, feel free to reach out to Khyle Hannan – Entrepreneurship Program Manager- Northeastern University Library .   Qualiﬁcations Minimum Qualiﬁcations BA or BS degree Experience or demonstrated interest working with Entrepreneurship or related Business ﬁelds in an academic setting Knowledge of business or entrepreneurial resources, methodologies, research trends and pedagogical approaches related to business and entrepreneurship Excellent communication, presentation, interpersonal and organizational skills, including strong time-management skills.   Preferred Qualiﬁcations ALA-accredited master's degree in library/information science attained or in process of completion, or advanced degree in education/teaching or business-related ﬁeld Previous teaching or public speaking experience Strong skills in community outreach, networking and building relationships   Job Duties 50% Subject Librarian / Liaison - Liaise to the D’Amore-McKim School of Business serving as a key resource for their faculty, students, and research staff in order to advance the library’s integration into teaching, learning, and scholarship activities. Teaching, Learning, and Research Support Collaborate with faculty to design and deliver course-based workshops on information literacy Provide open workshops on citation tools, discovery tools, and other knowledge areas/tools supporting the curriculum Partner with liaisons to develop online learning objects, research guides, and other web resources Provide online and in-person research support such as scheduled consultations, walk-in research help, classroom instruction, or virtual assistance. Partner with staff across the library to support research data management, scholarly publishing, repository services, as well as emerging researcher resources and tools.   Outreach Maintain frequent, ongoing communication with faculty and researchers in assigned disciplines to actively support teaching, research and promote library services and initiatives. Attend in-person and virtual campus events   Collection Development Evaluate and select materials in assigned disciplines appropriate to meet the needs of the university. Recommend budget levels and expend allotted budgets. Evaluate collections to meet program, accreditation, and grant activities   25% Entrepreneurship Support - Provides specialized, interdisciplinary support to entrepreneurship activities across the Northeastern University community in order to incorporate library resources and services into this strategic initiative. Builds relationships, monitors trends, and develops an interdisciplinary program that supports the evolving needs of entrepreneurship curricula and programs Serve as a subject matter expert within the library, collaborating with liaisons on critical elements to facilitate engagement around entrepreneurship Support collection development efforts in entrepreneurship as needed 15% Northeastern University Community Service - Be an active member of the Northeastern University community by participating, contributing, or volunteering on university or library committees, teams, working groups, projects, or initiatives that further the mission of the university.   10% Professional Development - Keep abreast of developments and trends in academic librarianship, business, entrepreneurship and higher education in general. Participate in Library, University, and/or other organizations, forums and conferences as appropriate.   We acknowledge that lists of skills and experience may overlook qualities that would most strengthen our team. We encourage candidates to speak about their experience and knowledge and tell us how it may connect to some of the qualiﬁcations for this position.  Position Type Library Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Manager--Accommodations---Leaves_R143074-1": {
      "title": "Manager- Accommodations & Leaves",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary: Reporting to the Associate Vice-President, Total Rewards, Global Mobility and Compliance, the Manager, Accommodations & Leaves (Canada) leads Northeastern University’s accommodations and leave programs across its U.S. and Canadian locations. For the Canadian campuses in Toronto and Vancouver, the Manager directly manages both workplace accommodations and leaves of absence, ensuring compliance with the Ontario and British Columbia Human Rights Codes, the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA), provincial employment standards legislation, and university policy. For the U.S., the Manager oversees the accommodations program delivered through a direct report (ADA Specialist) in adherence to the ADAAA, the PWFA, Massachusetts Chapter 151B, and other applicable state and local law. Leaves of absence in both countries are administered by the university’s third-party vendor; U.S. leave administration is fully outsourced. The Manager, Accommodations & Leaves serves as the university’s primary point of accountability for that vendor, overseeing service quality, the internal administrative work that supports each leave, and the accuracy of leave-related payments. The Manager partners closely with HR Business Partners, Payroll, Benefits, Talent Acquisition, and the Office of General Counsel. Responsibilities: Accommodations Program Management (U.S. & Canada): Directly manages the disability and pregnancy-related accommodations process for Canadian faculty, staff, and applicants, engaging in the interactive process, reviewing medical documentation, and issuing written determinations and individual accommodation plans to the point of undue hardship. Oversees the U.S. accommodations program delivered by the ADA Specialist, serving as the escalation point for complex, high-risk, or precedent-setting cases. Ensures decisions are individualized, consistent across both countries, and fully documented in the system of record. Partners with Talent Acquisition to support applicants who require accommodations during recruitment. Leave Administration & Vendor Oversight (U.S. & Canada): Serves as the primary internal liaison with the university’s third-party leave administrator for U.S. and Canadian leaves, monitoring performance against contractual SLAs, auditing claim decisions and data, and escalating and resolving discrepancies. For the fully outsourced U.S. program, oversees the internal administrative entries in Workday and the accuracy of leave-related payments, partnering with Payroll and Benefits on reconciliation, corrections, and overpayment recovery. For Canada, manages leaves end to end, including job-protected statutory leaves under the Ontario and BC Employment Standards Acts, short- and long-term disability claims, Records of Employment, and any salary top-up or benefit continuation. Compliance, Policy & Training: Monitors U.S. federal and state and Canadian federal and provincial legislation, regulatory changes, and case law affecting accommodations and leave, and recommends updates to university policies, procedures, and communications. Supports AODA employment-standard obligations, including individual accommodation plans, individualized workplace emergency response information, and documented return-to-work processes. Delivers training to managers, HR Business Partners, and university partners in both countries. Produces reporting on case volume, vendor performance, and payment accuracy to identify process improvements. Return to Work & Case Coordination: Coordinates return-to-work and graduated return plans for Canadian employees, aligning leave, disability claim, and accommodations outcomes, and ensures U.S. accommodations and leave outcomes are coordinated at return to work. Manages the intersection of accommodations with workplace injury claims under WSIB and WorkSafeBC and refers U.S. workers’ compensation matters to the appropriate office. Tracks leave exhaustion and LTD transitions, escalating complex cases to the AP, Total Rewards, Global Mobility and Compliance and the Office of General Counsel. People Leadership: Supervises the ADA Specialist, including caseload management, quality review of determinations, coaching, and performance and development planning. Sets consistent standards, templates, and workflows for the accommodation and leave programs. Serves as backup for U.S. accommodation casework as needed. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Education & Experience Knowledge and skills typically acquired through a Bachelor’s degree in human resources, disability management, psychology, social work, or a related field, plus 5–7 years of progressive experience in workplace accommodations, disability management, and/or leave administration, including casework in both the U.S. and Canada. At least two years of experience supervising or leading staff. Experience overseeing a third-party leave or disability claims administrator, including SLA monitoring, auditing, payment reconciliation, and escalation management. Required Knowledge & Skills Working knowledge of U.S. accommodations and leave law, including the ADAAA, the PWFA, the FMLA, Massachusetts Chapter 151B, Massachusetts Paid Family and Medical Leave, and other applicable state and local requirements. Working knowledge of the duty to accommodate under the Ontario and British Columbia Human Rights Codes; the AODA and its Integrated Accessibility Standards Regulation (IASR); the Ontario and BC Employment Standards Acts; Employment Insurance special benefits; and WSIB / WorkSafeBC. Ability to interpret medical and functional-abilities documentation and communicate clearly with treating providers, employees, and managers. Strong understanding of how leave status drives pay, benefits, and payroll processing, with the analytical skills to identify and resolve payment discrepancies. Sound judgment and discretion in handling sensitive and confidential information. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage competing priorities across two countries. Excellent written and oral communication skills, including drafting determination letters and training content. Ability to build collaborative relationships and influence stakeholders at all levels across U.S. and Canadian teams. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel); Workday experience a plus. Preferred CHRP/CHRL, Certified Disability Management Professional (CDMP), Certified Return to Work Coordinator (CRTWC), or ADA Coordinator certification Experience in higher education or a multi-state / multi-country organization. Position Type Human Resources Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 110S Expected Hiring Range: $76,335.00 - $107,823.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Associate-Research-Scientist_R143032": {
      "title": "Associate Research Scientist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Khoury College of Computer Sciences Khoury College is committed to building a diverse and inclusive community among students, faculty and staff. We strongly encourage applicants from underrepresented groups, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and those with diverse experiences and backgrounds. We invite you to join a fast-moving, ambitious college with an underlying mission that is driven by our motto of “CS for Everyone.” About the Gyori Lab for Computational Biomedicine The Gyori Lab for Computational Biomedicine at Northeastern University builds systems that accelerate scientific discovery by combining artificial intelligence with human expertise. The lab develops knowledge-grounded artificial intelligence (AI), text mining and knowledge assembly, mathematical and systems modeling, and causal analysis, and deploys its results as widely used open-source software and services. The lab’s work is supported by a portfolio of federal and foundation grants spanning biomedical knowledge integration, global health, and machine-assisted systems modeling. More information about the lab and its projects is available at https://gyorilab.github.io. Job Summary The Associate Research Scientist will work in a fully grant-funded position focused on advancing the goals and deliverables of the lab’s funded projects. Working within defined project objectives and timelines, the scientist will develop and implement computational methods and open-source scientific software in the areas of knowledge-grounded AI, systems modeling, natural language processing, and data harmonization. The scientist will also build domain-relevant applications to benchmark and showcase these methods, contribute to publications and presentations describing the work, and help guide graduate students and other junior team members. Because the position is fully supported by project funding, its scope and continuation are tied to the objectives and duration of the associated grants. The position reports to Benjamin Gyori, Associate Professor, and is based in Boston, Massachusetts. Minimum Qualifications Required PhD or equivalent Extensive and progressively responsible experience leading and contributing to computational research projects, including the ability to plan and execute research Track record of performance on research programs, peer-reviewed publications, open-source software, and conference or seminar presentations Deep expertise in one or more of the following areas, or a combination thereof: Knowledge-grounded AI and knowledge graphs, including large language model (LLM) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approaches Systems and mathematical modeling of biological or complex systems Natural language processing and machine learning Data harmonization and integration, particularly for biomedical applications Strong scientific software development skills Commitment to reproducible, open research practices Ability to deliver defined project goals Previous supervisory experience and the ability to guide graduate students, junior scientists, and other junior team members Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Perform Research (60%) Develop and implement computational methods and open-source scientific software in knowledge-grounded AI, systems modeling, natural language processing, and data harmonization Build domain-relevant applications to benchmark and showcase computational methods Plan and execute research within defined project objectives and timelines Write for Publication (20%) Contribute to peer-reviewed publications and presentations describing the research Supervise Graduate Students (10%) Guide graduate students, junior scientists, and other junior team members in their work Draft New Grants (5%) Contribute to drafting new grant proposals Purchasing and Budget Administration (5%) Perform purchasing and budget administration activities supporting the lab’s research Required Documents Resume Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Portland-ME/Part-Time-Lecturer---Analytics--Portland-_R143046-1": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer - Analytics (Portland)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Professional Studies at Northeastern University invites applications for a non-tenure track part time faculty lecturer in Analytics on the Portland campus. The College of Professional Studies is one of ten colleges of Northeastern University, a nationally ranked private research university. Founded in 1960, the College provides lifelong experiential learning that unleashes the capacities of aspiring individuals in all stages and walks of life. The College teaches undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students on campus and online in more than 90 programs.  Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Responsibilities Qualified candidates must be prepared to work with global student populations. Instructional areas included, but are not limited to, analytics, with particular expertise in probability and statistics, data exploration, data visualization, , database management systems, leadership and risk management in analytics, business support and predictive analytics. The mission of the Master of Professional Studies in Analytics program is to foster foundational analytics skills among working professionals, including preparing data, conducting data analysis, forecasting, optimization, data visualization, and data storytelling. This degree prepares students for entry and mid-level roles in analytics, such as data analyst, data specialist, database analyst, program analyst, research analyst, or research associate. These roles are general analyst roles and are not specific to any particular professional domains or disciplines (e.g., business, marketing, and engineering). The degree is deeply rooted in experiential learning that is closely linked to professional applications in the workforce. Qualifications Minimum qualification: Masters in an aligned discipline and analytics-industry experience. Preference for candidates with a PhD in a sciences field, or similar. Demonstration of teaching, coaching, and/or training is required, with a history of successful teaching (online/on ground) at the graduate level is strongly preferred Application Materials Applicants should submit materials including a cover letter and vitae. Successful faculty at Northeastern will be dynamic and innovative scholars with a record of teaching excellence and a commitment to fostering belonging in the university community. Thus, strong candidates for this faculty position will have the expertise, knowledge, and skills to build their pedagogy, and curriculum in ways that reflect and enhance this commitment. Please indicate how your expertise, knowledge, and skills have prepared you to contribute to this work in your cover letter. Please direct questions to Prashant Mittal at p.mittal@northeastern.edu. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit $2,086.44."
    },
