      "title": "ECE Part-Time Lecturer - Artificial Intelligence (Silicon Valley)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Opportunity Northeastern University’s Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering invites applicants for a non-tenure track part-time faculty position to teach in the Master of Science in Artificial Intelligence, located on-ground at the Silicon Valley campus in San Jose, CA. The MS in Artificial Intelligence prepares future leaders in AI with the essential skills to design and implement AI systems, offering a concentration in computer vision in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering. Responsibilities Teach selected master’s-level courses in the Master of Science in Artificial Intelligence program in the College of Engineering (COE) at Northeastern University’s Silicon Valley campus. Course topics include Introductory Machine Learning, Linear Algebra for Machine Learning, and Statistical Inference. Responsibilities include course preparation (lectures, course materials, examinations, etc.), teaching in person, and evaluation of student performance in the course. Qualifications M.S. or Ph.D. in a related discipline is required; some professional and/or teaching experience preferred. Must have strong written and verbal skills to communicate well with students. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Key responsibilities include class notes preparation and class teaching time; holding office hours; homework, quiz, and exam preparation; homework, quiz, and exam grading; and weekly/periodic coordination meetings with the Director of Global Programs in Electrical & Computer Engineering and Boston campus representatives/instructors. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer. The salary listed for this position is the per-credit rate of $2,693.75; total compensation is based on the number of credits taught. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $2,693.75."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Portland-ME/Financial-Analyst---Roux-Institute_R143110": {
      "title": "Financial Analyst - Roux Institute",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled analyst to support the financial operations of Northeastern University’s Roux Institute. The ideal candidate will have prior experience in higher education and possess a deep understanding of financial analysis, data interpretation, and reporting. The primary focus of this role will be to support the institute’s financial and business operations by providing accurate, timely, and relevant information to key stakeholders. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to effectively communicate to audiences at all levels of the organization, translating for both technical and non-technical audiences. Produce and deliver succinct, compelling materials. Knowledge of finance and accounting principles. Excellent analytical, problem solving, decision-making, and time management skills with a high attention to detail. Strong proficiency in Excel and ability to learn custom ERP systems. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Knowledge and skills are normally acquired through completion of a Bachelor's Degree in a business or finance discipline and two to five years' experience in a financial analysis role.  Knowledge of a higher educational environment is preferred. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACCOUNTABILITIES Financial Analysis Conduct regular financial analysis and modeling to support regular business functions, strategic planning, budgeting, forecasting and decision making processes for the institute.  Monitor and analyze key financial indicators such as revenue, expense, and cash flow to identify trends and variances. Prepare and present financial reports and presentations to senior management, department heads, and other stakeholders. Assist unit leaders with actively managing their area in terms of revenue generation and tracking current expenditures.  Analyze financial and payroll discrepancies to ensure timely corrections. Collaborate with other departments within the organization, including enrollment, marketing, and learner services to ensure alignment of financial goals and objectives. Assist the research teams with management of funding awards, ensuring compliance with award terms and conditions. Modeling and Reporting Lead the continued development and refinement of the institute’s 10-year business model. Assist with the development and creation of annual reporting data for senior leadership, board of trustees, and institute donors. Assist with translating team goals into actionable and trackable financial metrics. Conduct market research and competitive analysis to inform the institute’s pricing and financial strategies. Conduct ad-hoc financial analysis to support the institute’s business operations. Other Duties Assist with analyzing existing processes to improve workflow and work efficiencies.  Develop and implement financial policies and procedures to ensure compliance with organizational and regulatory requirements. Assist in developing new financial analysis and reporting capabilities for the institute. Provide financial training and support to staff and faculty members with varying degrees of financial acumen. Create strong relationships with university colleagues and actively collaborate with them to help strengthen Northeastern’s global network. Provide support and backup to other team members. Provide support for special projects and other duties as assigned. Review and approve expense reports in Concur, ensuring accurate coding and complete documentation. AP/AR process to ensure timely and accurate payments and receivables. Position Type Finance Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Assistant--Associate--Full-Professor--Colleges-of-Science-and-Engineering--Quantum-Science-and-Technology_R143077": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, Full Professor, Colleges of Science and Engineering, Quantum Science and Technology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About Northeastern: Founded in 1898, Northeastern is a global research university and the recognized leader in experience-driven lifelong learning. Our world-renowned experiential approach empowers our students, faculty, alumni, and partners to create impact far beyond the confines of discipline, degree, and campus. Our locations—in Arlington; Boston; Charlotte, North Carolina; London; Miami; New York City; Oakland; Portland, Maine; Seattle; Silicon Valley; Toronto; Vancouver; and the Massachusetts communities of Burlington and Nahant—are nodes in our growing global university system. Through this network, we expand opportunities for flexible, student-centered learning and collaborative, solutions-focused research. Northeastern’s comprehensive array of undergraduate and graduate programs—in a variety of on-campus and online formats—lead to degrees through the doctorate in nine colleges and schools. Among these, we offer more than 195 multi-discipline majors and degrees designed to prepare students for purposeful lives and careers. The College of Science comprises six departments: Biology, Chemistry and Chemical Biology, Marine and Environmental Sciences, Mathematics, Physics, and Psychology. The Department of Physics ( https://cos.northeastern.edu/physics/ ) includes 51 tenured/tenure-track faculty, 14 full-time teaching faculty; four research faculty; and one professor of the practice. Physics enrolls over 100 undergraduate physics majors, over 200 physics majors combined with other majors, and over 100 PhD students. The College of Engineering comprises six departments: Bioengineering, Chemical Engineering, Civil and Environmental Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Mechanical and Industrial Engineering, and Software Engineering and Information Systems. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering ( https://ece.northeastern.edu/ ) includes 89 tenured/tenure track faculty, 8 research faculty, and 14 teaching faculty. ECE has around 950 undergraduate students, 600 master’s students and 325 Ph.D. students. About the Opportunity: Northeastern University seeks exceptional faculty candidates to establish transformative research programs at the frontiers of quantum science and technology with appointments in the College of Science ( https://cos.northeastern.edu/ ) and/or the College of Engineering ( https://coe.northeastern.edu/ ), and becoming a core member of Northeastern’s Quantum Materials and Sensing Institute ( https://quantum.northeastern.edu/ ). We welcome applicants across the full spectrum of quantum science and technology encompassing experimental, theoretical, and computational areas, including research at the intersection of quantum science and AI/ML, at all ranks (Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor) to fill up to three positions . Successful candidates will have tenure homes in Physics or Electrical and Computer Engineering beginning in academic year 2027-2028, with the possibility of joint appointments with other departments. Areas of interest include (but are not limited to): 1. Quantum networking and communication: Theory of coherent quantum information transfer across physical platforms, spanning quantum communication and networking protocols, light-matter interactions, quantum optical frameworks for photon generation and entanglement in excitonic and photonic systems, and Hamiltonian engineering for materials-level quantum phenomena. Areas of expertise include condensed matter systems, quantum optics, quantum information theory, topology, group theory, quantum field theory, photonic integrated circuit design, microwave quantum engineering, signal processing, AI/ML-guided design, and materials platforms that underpin photon coherence and control. 2. Quantum sensing, navigation and precision timing: Experiments on quantum-coherent systems, including spin qubits, topological electron states, and entangled photon fields as precision probes of quantum matter.  Investigation of atomic-scale electromagnetic fields using Berry curvature-enhanced orbital responses, and of macroscopic inertial forces using quantum entanglement and matter-wave interferometry, to achieve sensitivities inaccessible to classical instrumentation. Areas of expertise include quantum measurement platforms, condensed matter, atomic and optical physics, precision instrumentation, microwave and RF systems, sensor design, quantum materials and heterostructures, and AI/ML-guided materials discovery. 3. Next-Generation Quantum Computing: Quantum Algorithms and Intelligent Computing Systems : Topics span quantum computing, quantum computer architecture, quantum computer engineering, broadly defined. We welcome researchers advancing quantum algorithms and systems, quantum processors and architectures, hardware–software co-design, scalable computing platforms, AI-assisted quantum systems, heterogeneous architectures, intelligent computing infrastructure, and scalable computing platforms. Candidates with interdisciplinary expertise spanning computing systems, AI, robotics, quantum technologies, and emerging hardware platforms are especially encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will join the Quantum Materials and Sensing Institute https://quantum.northeastern.edu/ ), and leverage the Institute for NanoSystems Innovation ( https://nanosi.northeastern.edu/ ), the Kostas Research Institute ( https://kostas.northeastern.edu/ ), our world-class laboratories such as the Experiential Quantum Advancement Laboratories (EQUAL,  https://equal.sites.northeastern.edu/ ) and other quantum laboratories and facilities including state-of-the-art clean room synthesis, characterization, and fabrication tools, ultrafast optical spectroscopy, cryogenic measurement systems, quantum transport tools, and high-performance computing clusters. Selected candidates will advance quantum science and technology in support of Northeastern’s broader strategic vision of use-inspired research in health, security, and sustainability, active industry engagement, and the development of quantum education and workforce programs. Our tenure and promotion process values collaborative research and teamwork. Hires will be mentored for success, with mentoring teams and group guidance. In addition, a strong and effective faculty development strategy is part of the Northeastern institutional mission. The ADVANCE Office of Faculty Development office works in conjunction with the Office of Research Development (ORD), the Office of Belonging, the Center for Advancing Teaching and Learning Through Research (CATLR), and University Decision Support (UDS) to provide programs and trainings to further develop and support a thriving faculty. Responsibilities: Successful candidates will develop vigorous, independent research programs cutting across physics, electrical engineering, and other science and engineering disciplines, and attract external funding. Faculty at Northeastern are expected to teach courses at the graduate and undergraduate levels, supervise students and postdocs in their areas of research, and participate in service to the department, university, and discipline. Candidates joining the Quantum Materials and Sensing Institute will collaborate on multi-faculty, mission-driven research programs at the frontiers of quantum science and engineering. These positions will be based in Boston, Massachusetts and/or Burlington, Massachusetts. Because Northeastern has many campuses spread across the globe beyond its main campus in Boston, qualified candidates must be prepared to work with our worldwide student population. Qualifications: A Ph.D., or equivalent, in physics, engineering, a quantum-related discipline, or a relevant interdisciplinary area is required by the employment start date. We encourage applicants from a wide range of backgrounds, including academia and industry. Applicants must demonstrate a strong record of scholarly accomplishments and the potential to establish a world-class, externally funded research program. Postdoctoral experience is not required for appointment at the Assistant Professor level. Candidates seeking appointment at the Associate Professor level should have at least 4 years of experience and at the Full Professor level of at least 8 years of academic or equivalent experience (e.g. industry research) with strong track record of external grant support and academic leadership. Additional Information: How to apply: Interested candidates should apply using the Northeastern University website. Applicants should indicate their area(s) of interest in the cover letter, including interest in joint appointments with other departments or colleges. Applications must include the following: (1) a cover letter; (2) a curriculum vita that includes a full list of publications; (3) statements addressing the prompts below; and (4) names and contact information for at least three professional references from whom letters of reference may be solicited. Successful faculty at Northeastern will be dynamic and innovative scholars with a record of research and teaching excellence and a commitment to fostering belonging in the university community. Thus, strong candidates for this faculty position will have the expertise, knowledge, and skills to build their research, pedagogy, and curriculum in ways that reflect and enhance this commitment. Please indicate how your expertise, knowledge, and skills have prepared you to contribute to this work with written statements addressing the following prompts: Research statement (no longer than 5 pages): Describe the focus area(s) of your research, including the major scientific questions you have addressed, the funding you have received to support the work (if applicable), and the major discoveries you have made. Highlight any cross-disciplinary research efforts you have undertaken. Also comment on any research you have undertaken with students and/or with the external community.   Finally, provide an overview of the research directions you foresee pursuing at Northeastern, including cross-disciplinary and collaborative aspects of your research. Teaching statement (1 page ): Summarize your past instructional and mentorship experience, pedagogical philosophy, plans/goals for teaching in the College of Science or the College of Engineering (including existing and proposed courses), and your strategies for teaching and mentoring Northeastern’s global student populations as appropriate. Leadership statement (1 page): Describe your past experience and activities, if appropriate, and future plans  your leadership style, how you intend to cultivate a culture that promotes a sense of belonging, including fostering a free and open exchange of ideas and managing different perspectives to help others strengthen their practice. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, as they are received. The review will continue until the position is filled. Inquiries should be directed to Professor Arun Bansil ( ar.bansil@northeastern.edu ), Search Committee Chair. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: Assistant Professor: $111,000.00 - $137,000.00 | Associate Professor: $116,000.00 - $168,000.00 | Professor: $132,000.00 - $271,000.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Oakland-CA/Adjunct-Faculty---Art---Design_R142925-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Art + Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The College of Arts, Media and Design at Northeastern University seeks applicants to teach in-person undergraduate courses in Art + Design at the Oakland campus in Oakland, California for the upcoming Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 semesters. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Adjunct Faculty will hold office hours as appropriate. Qualifications: The ideal candidate will have an MFA or equivalent terminal degree and at least two years of successful college teaching experience. Art, media arts and design candidates should have active careers with current exhibition, publication, or creative practice and course related experience. Candidates must have the ability to effectively engage Northeastern students at course relevant levels of study, whether beginning, intermediate or advanced. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future. Furthermore, the successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University’s sponsorship for a visa. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The per credit rate starts at $2,484.48"
