    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Miami-FL/Campus-Assistant--Miami_R143062": {
      "title": "Campus Assistant- Miami",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Campus Assistant – Miami Part-Time Temporary (5 -15 Hrs/Wk)   Northeastern University–Miami is seeking an energetic, organized professional for the Campus Assistant position (part-time temporary). The Campus Assistant will be responsible for staffing the campus during the day and/or assisting with evening and weekend class meetings, study hours, and special events. Primary duties include, greeting guests and students providing general university information, ensuring instructor’s needs are met to begin class, troubleshooting technology issues, managing room setup for classes, ensuring cleanliness and order of Kitchenette area, and assisting students with their requests. The Campus Assistant will also be assigned administrative or other projects as needed.     Associate’s degree required, Bachelor's degree preferred along with 2 years of professional office experience (administrative or customer support), preferably in higher education. The successful candidate will have outstanding customer service and problem-solving skills. Strong organizational and communication skills, both verbal and written, are critical to this role. Must be extremely detail-oriented and able to prioritize work to meet campus and client expectations. Must have the ability to make sound decisions and judgments to best serve clients’ needs and meet campus goals. Proficiency in Word, Excel, and other Microsoft Office Suite necessary, as well as familiarity with using audio/video equipment and other technology.   Hours   ·        Morning and Evening hours during the semester as needed. ·        Some weekends. ·        Schedule is dependent on term and campus activities.   Key Responsibilities   ·        Greet and assist students, faculty, and guests Field questions from student, faculty, and guests, ensuring ·        appropriate resolution Provide technical support and other customer service for students and faculty ·        Security and Maintenance of Campus ·        Respond to and document evening maintenance requests Ensure campus areas used are clean and ready to begin the next working day before leaving; inform custodial staff of any special needs Stock supplies in classroom, kitchen/lounge, etc. Assume primary responsibility for the application of the Miami campus’ emergency procedures; coordinate with faculty and building security in cases of inclement weather or emergencies ·        Conduct complete check of campus before departure; ensure all equipment and lights are powered down and secure doors ·        Event Support ·        Support student services events as needed Assist with student orientations   Other Special Projects (i.e. website audits, update databases, inventories, web research)   Position Type Temporary Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. This job is for a current or anticipated job vacancy. Pay Rate: $18/hour"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Seattle-WA/Program-Manager_R143138": {
      "title": "Program Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity The Program Manager serves as the senior administrative and operational leader for the Northeastern University Seattle Physician Assistant Program and works in close partnership with the Program Director to establish and advance the program's operational priorities. As a founding member of the Seattle PA Program team, this position will develop and implement the systems, policies, procedures, and workflows necessary to support the development, accreditation, launch, and ongoing operations of the program. Embodying a growth mindset and approaching operations as a form of customer service, the Program Manager will build clear, effective, and sustainable systems that enable faculty and staff to do their best work and contribute to an exceptional student experience. The position will continuously assess program operations, identify opportunities for improvement, and develop solutions that promote efficiency, collaboration, responsiveness, and program quality. The Program Manager provides leadership for the administrative functions of the program, including supervision and development of program staff; admissions operations; major program events and activities; program records, data, and administrative systems; and operational support for accreditation and program evaluation. The Program Manager also serves as a key administrative partner to the Program Director, supporting the coordination of strategic priorities, complex meetings and initiatives, and other activities requiring collaboration across the program, university, and external partners. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree and a minimum of 5–7 years of progressively responsible experience in higher education, academic program administration, healthcare administration, business operations, project management, or a related professional setting. Demonstrated experience managing complex programs, projects, or operational processes. Demonstrated supervisory or team leadership experience. Experience developing and implementing policies, procedures, workflows, or administrative systems. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Excellent organizational, written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong leadership and supervisory skills, including the ability to develop, motivate, and support a high-performing team. Demonstrated growth mindset and commitment to continuous improvement. Strong strategic planning, project management, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Ability to translate strategic priorities into effective operational plans, processes, and systems. Ability to anticipate needs, exercise sound independent judgment, and appropriately prioritize and escalate issues. Ability to manage multiple concurrent priorities and meet deadlines in a dynamic environment. Strong attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Demonstrated service orientation and ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, university partners, and external stakeholders. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and ability to learn and effectively utilize university information systems and other technology platforms. Experience in health professions education, admissions, accreditation, or academic program administration preferred. Familiarity with Physician Assistant education and ARC-PA accreditation requirements preferred.   Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities   Operational Effectiveness – 30% Develop, implement, and continuously improve administrative systems, policies, procedures, protocols, and workflows that support effective operation of the Seattle PA Program. Oversee daily program operations, including program records and databases, communications, scheduling, purchasing, facilities coordination, and other administrative functions. Partner with the Program Director in the development and administration of the program budget, including tracking expenditures, monitoring budget performance, preparing reports and projections, coordinating purchasing and financial transactions, and supporting annual and long-range budget planning. Develop and maintain systems to track recurring program processes, deadlines, requirements, and deliverables and ensure appropriate follow-through. Use data, feedback, and continuous quality improvement principles to identify operational gaps, anticipate program needs, and develop scalable solutions as the program grows. Facilitate communication and collaboration among faculty, staff, students, university offices, and external partners. Collaborate with the Program Director to identify opportunities to enhance program operations and implement strategies to improve effectiveness and the student, faculty, and staff experience.   Leadership and Management – 20% Build and lead a high-performing administrative team and provide direct supervision, mentorship, and professional development for program staff. Establish clear roles, responsibilities, workflows, performance expectations, and priorities for administrative staff. Oversee staff projects and daily workflow; delegate responsibilities; monitor progress; and provide clear, ongoing feedback and performance management. Foster a positive team culture grounded in collaboration, service, accountability, innovation, and continuous improvement. Lead regular administrative staff meetings and coordinate administrative work across the program to ensure alignment with faculty and program leadership priorities. Participate in recruitment, hiring, onboarding, training, and evaluation of program administrative staff.   Admissions & Student Program Administration – 20% Provide administrative leadership for the Seattle PA Program admissions process in collaboration with the Program Director, faculty leadership, and university admissions offices. Develop, implement, and oversee admissions workflows, timelines, applicant communications, application processing, interview activities, records, and data management. Provide operational leadership for admissions events and interview days and ensure efficient, consistent, and equitable administrative processing throughout the admissions cycle. Coordinate administrative processes associated with matriculation, student onboarding, orientation, and maintenance of student records. Serve as a key administrative resource for students and collaborate with faculty and university offices to facilitate resolution of administrative and operational issues. Ensure applicant- and student-facing administrative processes and communications are consistent with university policies and applicable accreditation requirements.   Program Events, Accreditation, and Compliance – 15% Provide leadership and operational oversight for major program events, including admissions events, student orientation, White Coat Ceremony, graduation activities, faculty retreats, and other program functions. Develop event timelines and oversee facilities, vendors, communications, materials, invitations, and other logistics necessary for successful execution. Coordinate administrative logistics for accreditation activities, including preparation for accreditation reviews and site visits. Support accreditation, program evaluation, and continuous self-study through coordination of documentation, data collection, reporting, and records management. Collaborate with program leadership to ensure administrative processes, records, and program communications remain consistent with university requirements and applicable accreditation standards.   Strategic Program and Program Director Support – 15% Serve as a key administrative and operational partner to the Program Director in advancing program priorities, strategic initiatives, and special projects. Develop and maintain systems for tracking major projects, decisions, deadlines, and action items and proactively identify matters requiring Program Director attention or follow-up. Coordinate complex or high-level meetings and initiatives involving program faculty and staff, university leadership, candidates, external partners, and other key stakeholders, including scheduling, logistics, agendas, materials, and follow-up. Provide targeted calendar and scheduling support to the Program Director to facilitate effective prioritization and coordination of major meetings, initiatives, and external engagements. Translate Program Director priorities into operational plans, timelines, and deliverables and coordinate implementation across relevant program stakeholders. Represent the Seattle PA Program on university committees, working groups, and administrative meetings as appropriate. Lead or coordinate special projects as assigned by the Program Director.   Financial Measures Annual operating budget managed: To be determined Partners with the Program Director in development, administration, monitoring, and forecasting of the Seattle PA Program operating budget.   Supervision Direct reports are anticipated to include a Didactic Manager, Clinical Manager, and student, temporary, or other administrative personnel as assigned.   Position Type Academic Administration Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 107H Expected Hiring Range: $25.78 - $39.95 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Lab-Manager_R143099": {
      "title": "Lab Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Khoury College of Computer Sciences Khoury College is committed to building a community of belonging among students, faculty and staff. We strongly encourage applicants from individuals with disabilities, veterans, and those with varied experiences and backgrounds. We invite you to join a fast-moving, ambitious college with an underlying mission that is driven by our motto of “CS for Everyone.” About the Opportunity The Bau Lab Manager supports the day-to-day operations of David Bau’s interpretability lab at Northeastern University’s Khoury College of Computer Sciences and the National Deep Inference Fabric (NDIF), a National Science Foundation-funded open research platform for artificial intelligence. This generalist operations role works across academic research and large-scale infrastructure, managing multiple priorities while anticipating needs and keeping projects moving. Responsibilities may include managing budgets and reimbursements, planning workshops, coordinating hiring activities, and supporting grant proposals. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Finance and Administration: Track and manage budgets across multiple grants, process purchasing and reimbursements, and maintain organized spending records Events and Logistics: Plan and execute events, including the New England Mechanistic Interpretability (NEMI) Workshop and other gatherings; secure venues, reserve rooms, arrange travel and catering, and coordinate on-site logistics Hiring and Onboarding: Coordinate recruitment activities for staff, students, and research roles; work with Northeastern University Human Resources to post positions, schedule interviews, and onboard new lab members Grant Proposals: Manage the grant proposal process, including tracking deadlines, assembling and formatting materials, and coordinating with collaborators and Northeastern University research administrators Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience Experience in research administration, operations, event planning, or office management Experience working with budgets, purchasing, and basic financial tracking Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently, take ownership, and follow through with minimal oversight Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Research-Engineer_R143103": {
      "title": "Research Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Khoury College of Computer Sciences Khoury College is committed to building a community of belonging among students, faculty and staff. We strongly encourage applicants from individuals with disabilities, veterans, and those with varied experiences and backgrounds. We invite you to join a fast-moving, ambitious college with an underlying mission that is driven by our motto of “CS for Everyone.” About the Opportunity The Security and Privacy Heterogeneous Environment for Reproducible Experimentation (SPHERE) is a newly funded National Science Foundation (NSF) mid-scale research infrastructure being built by the University of Southern California Information Sciences Institute and Northeastern University’s Khoury College of Computer Sciences. This research infrastructure will offer access to an unprecedented variety of hardware, software, and other resources relevant to cybersecurity and privacy research. These resources will be connected by a user-configurable network substrate and protected by security policies uniquely aligned with cybersecurity and privacy research needs. The Research Engineer will help build this innovative cyberinfrastructure. The portion of SPHERE being developed at Northeastern University will focus on Internet of Things (IoT) device experimentation. The primary goal is to create the world’s largest remotely accessible IoT testbed, composed of dozens of samples of IoT devices across several categories and manufacturers, including smart speakers, smart televisions, and smart cameras. In addition to hosting IoT devices, the SPHERE IoT testbed will provide programming interfaces for interacting with devices through all available modalities, including physical access, companion application access, and voice access. These interfaces will be remotely accessible, allowing users worldwide to interact with devices and conduct experiments without purchasing devices or building their own infrastructure. The IoT testbed will be complemented by tools for capturing network traffic produced by the devices, securely storing data, integrating with the broader SPHERE research infrastructure, and streamlining automated and repeatable experiments at scale. This is a unique opportunity to join a vibrant team and conduct groundbreaking research supporting scalable, large-scale virtual access to diverse IoT hardware. This is a research position and is on-site at the Boston campus. Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education, and skills when extending an offer. Northeastern University provides a comprehensive benefits package for benefits-eligible employees, including medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness and life benefits, retirement benefits, and commuting and transportation benefits. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Software Development Activities (70%): Design, implement, test, document, and maintain SPHERE software Support Activities (20%): Prepare project documentation and periodic reports, coordinate with project partners, and prepare and present testing demonstrations Learning (10%): Acquire and broaden knowledge of the technologies and development tools used by SPHERE Minimum Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a closely related area; this requirement may be waived based on relevant software development work experience Fluency in at least one programming language Experience with Linux and software development tools, such as Git Resourcefulness, initiative, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team Preferred Experience or interest in system or network administration, the Internet of Things, and/or cybersecurity Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Designer_R143119": {
      "title": "Designer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity In this entry-level role, the Designer will apply a broad set of skills within the realm of project delivery from planning, design, construction, and project completion. As a member of the In-hHuse Design & Construction group (IHDC), the Designer will contribute to all projects under the team’s portfolio. The In-House Design & Construction group works on projects for all of the University’s colleges, departments, and divisions across the Global Network, including student lounges, dorms, dining halls, classrooms, library spaces, and office fit-outs. All projects are assigned to a Designer/Project Manager (D/PM) and Designer/Assistant Project Manager (D/APM), with the Designer acting as an additional resource to those project teams as needed. The Designer will collaborate with project teams on design and assist on activities such as creating architectural drawing sets, FF&E presentations and renderings, and documentation of existing conditions. The Designer will collaborate with Design Co-ops in the execution of those production needs, as well as create and maintain graphic standards to ensure quality control of deliverables. Other responsibilities include: CAD/BIM documentation of projects and existing site conditions; providing documentation and assistance in design development from schematic through construction documents phase; and assisting in specifying paint, flooring, lighting, and all associated finishes and furniture. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Preferred software knowledge: AutoCAD, Revit, Adobe Creative Suite Ability to read and interpret architectural documents Self-motivated problem solver with the ability to work independently on difficult and complex tasks while making sound decisions Knowledge and skills required for this role are often acquired through a vachelor’s degree plus 0-2 years of professional experience in architecture, interior design, and related fields. Minimum of four (4) years experience in lieu of professional degree. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES & ACCOUNTABILITIES: 1) Production of drawing sets, including construction drawings, assessments, test fits, and sketches as needed. This would be completed through the use of BIM, CAD, or hand-sketching as needed. 2) Assist, and in certain situations, lead furniture and finish specification of projects in design. This includes identifying options, preparing options into a presentable medium, and documenting appropriately. 3) Maintenance and definition of CAD/BIM standards as they related to design processes for the In-House Design and Construction team. 4) Ongoing maintenance and management of finish library, both in physical and digital mediums. Position Type Facilities Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 108S Expected Hiring Range: $60,315.00 - $85,192.50 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Chief-Financial-Officer_R143139-1": {
      "title": "Chief Financial Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Role The University seeks a Chief Financial Officer (CFO) to serve as its senior financial executive and to provide strategic and operational leadership for the institution's financial affairs. Reporting to the Senior Vice President, Finance & Administration, the CFO is responsible for the University's long-term financial sustainability, financial integrity, regulatory compliance, and prudent stewardship of resources in support of its academic, research, student, and institutional mission. Responsibilities The CFO oversees the development and execution of the University's financial strategy, including: Budgeting, forecasting, and financial planning and analysis Accounting and financial reporting Treasury and cash management Debt and capital planning Endowment leadership Tax compliance and reporting Procurement and payroll Internal controls and financial risk management The CFO partners closely with the President, the Board of Trustees and its Finance, Audit and Risk, and Investment Committees, and academic and administrative leaders to translate institutional priorities into sustainable financial strategies and decisions. The CFO serves as a strategic advisor to the President and University leadership, providing clear, timely, and actionable analysis of financial performance, risks, opportunities, and the long-term implications of institutional decisions. The CFO is also a principal representative of the University to external constituencies, including credit rating agencies, bondholders and the municipal securities market, external and federal auditors, banking and investment partners, donors, and regulatory agencies. Leadership Expectations The CFO fosters a culture of accountability, transparency, collaboration, and continuous improvement, and ensures compliance with applicable laws, regulations, accounting standards, and University policies. The successful candidate will model inclusive, collegial leadership and build a finance organization recognized across the institution for analytical rigor, service orientation, and integrity. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in finance, accounting, business administration, economics, or a related field Minimum of fifteen (15) years of progressively responsible financial management experience, including at least five (5) years leading a complex finance organization at a senior executive level Demonstrated experience in budgeting, financial planning and analysis, accounting, financial reporting, treasury and debt management, capital planning, endowment management, and financial risk management Experience advising senior executives and governing boards on complex financial matters, with the ability to translate technical financial information into clear, actionable guidance for non-financial audiences Experience managing significant budgets, financial resources, and organizational complexity within a decentralized, multi-unit enterprise Demonstrated ability to develop and execute long-term financial strategies, including multi-year financial modeling, scenario planning, and sensitivity analysis Experience with higher education financial models, including tuition revenue, enrollment forecasting, restricted funds, endowment resources and spending policy, sponsored research and facilities and administrative (F&A) cost recovery, financial aid discounting, auxiliaries, and capital financing Experience with institutional transformation, financial restructuring, or significant organizational change Senior financial leadership experience in higher education or another complex, mission-driven organization Position Type Finance Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 119S Expected Hiring Range: $376,385.00 - $559,872.50 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Research-Scientist_R143108": {
      "title": "Research Scientist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Northeastern University is seeking a highly motivated Research Scientist to lead computational modeling efforts investigating the effects of non-ionizing electromagnetic fields on the human nervous system. Working under the direction of Prof. Yarossi, this position will lead the development of realistic head models, tissue segmentation pipelines, and E-field simulations, as well as biophysical neuron modeling. The Research Scientist will collaborate closely with the Northeastern Center for Translational Neuroimaging and will supervise a Research Engineer and graduate student supporting the project. Responsibilities: Lead the creation of realistic head models for E-field simulation, including development of computational modeling pipelines. Conduct numerical simulations of neural activity using point models, cable models, and neural mass models. Implement biophysically realistic, multi-compartment neuron models to estimate electromagnetic field effects on neural tissue. Supervise and mentor the Research Engineer and graduate student on computational modeling tasks. Contribute to technical reporting, manuscript preparation, and dissemination of findings. Education/Experience: PhD in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Physics, or a closely related field. Demonstrated experience in computational modeling of electromagnetic fields in biological tissue and/or neuron modeling. Skills: Experience with E-field simulation platforms such as SimNIBS, Sim4Life, CST Studio Suite, or ANSYS HFSS. Experience with neuron modeling software such as NEURON, or with neural mass modeling approaches. Strong background in numerical methods, biophysical modeling, and simulation of neural dynamics. Prior experience modeling the effects of electromagnetic fields on biological tissue strongly preferred. Ability to independently lead technical work and mentor junior staff. Strong written and oral communication skills for scientific reporting and publication. In compliance with federal government contract requirements, U.S. citizenship is required for this role. Security clearance is not required.   Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Research-Engineer_R143107-1": {
      "title": "Research Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Northeastern University is seeking a motivated Research Engineer to support computational modeling and imaging efforts investigating the effects of non-ionizing electromagnetic fields on the human nervous system. Working under the direction of Prof. Yarossi, this position will support the development of head models and E-field simulations, working alongside the Research Scientist and in collaboration with the Northeastern Center for Translational Neuroimaging. Responsibilities: Support creation and segmentation of head models for E-field simulation. Assist in developing and applying computational modeling pipelines. Support neuron modeling efforts, including implementation and testing of multi-compartment models. Support imaging data processing and analysis in coordination with project collaborators. Contribute to technical reporting, documentation, and dissemination of project results. Education/Experience: BS required (MS preferred) in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Physics, or a closely related field. Experience with computational modeling, simulation, or imaging analysis is preferred. Skills: Familiarity with E-field simulation platforms such as SimNIBS, Sim4Life, CST Studio Suite, or ANSYS HFSS is a plus. Familiarity with neuron modeling tools such as NEURON, or neural mass modeling approaches, is a plus. Working knowledge of image segmentation and processing tools/pipelines (e.g., FreeSurfer, SPM, or similar) is beneficial. Solid programming and numerical computing skills (e.g., MATLAB, Python). Ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a multi-disciplinary research team. Strong attention to detail and interest in electromagnetic field effects on biological tissue. In compliance with federal government contract requirements, U.S. citizenship is required for this role. Security clearance is not required.   Position Type Research Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 109S Expected Hiring Range: $67,855.00 - $95,845.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Open-Rank-Teaching-Professor---MS-in-Human-Resources-Management_R137160": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor - MS in Human Resources Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Opportunity: The College of Professional Studies at Northeastern University invites applicants for a full-time faculty position in Human Resources Management. We seek a dedicated and dynamic individual to contribute to our innovative and forward-thinking programs in the field of Human Resources Management. The successful candidate will have a strong academic background, demonstrated research expertise, and significant industry experience as a practitioner in Human Resources Management. The position is a full-time, open rank, non-tenure track, renewable appointment located in Boston, MA. Responsibilities: This full-time faculty member is expected to bring her/his intellectual and creative capacity to bear in advancement of the program, seeking to serve students by participating in a range of teaching and non-teaching activities that support the advancement of the program. They will teach a full teaching load spread throughout the year and will work with the program office on administrative issues and programmatic projects. Faculty enjoy a collegial work environment that allows for work-life balance and are expected to be available to students online and in person as needed. Teaching and actual course load may vary with other responsibilities, which include, but are not limited to: Teaching & Curricular Oversight (approximately 80% of time) Teach a variety of graduate courses in Human Resources Management, including but not limited to topics such as talent acquisition, organizational development, compensation and benefits, employee relations, and strategic HR management. Engage in curriculum development, program assessment, and the integration of emerging HR trends and practices into academic offerings. Oversee the instruction of specific courses within the curriculum. Responsibilities include supporting the CPS Operations in the selection of part-time instructors, advising on syllabi, and evaluating part-time instructor performance. Mentor and advise students, guiding them in their academic and professional development. Establish and maintain collaborative relationships with industry partners, staying current on the latest HR trends and best practices. Service & Professional Development (approximately 20% of time) Create professional development opportunities for full and part-time faculty in the unit. Serve on committees that support the mission of the program and the vision of the College and wider University. Promote the discovery and dissemination of knowledge through scholarship, research, creative activity, and professional development. Faculty must demonstrate ongoing, substantive academic and/or professional engagement to ensure currency and relevancy within their field and to contribute to the institution’s mission, consistent with AACSB Standard. Travel In addition to supporting the campus, occasional travel may be required to the University’s global network of campuses. Examples of required travel include the annual CPS Graduation and Faculty Conference. Qualified candidates must be prepared to work with global student populations Qualifications: Terminal degree (Ph.D. or equivalent) in Management, Psychology, or a closely related discipline within Human Resources Management by appointment start date. Demonstrated record of scholarly achievement and professional engagement, including publications in reputable, peer-reviewed academic journals. Significant professional experience in Human Resources Management or a related field, ideally at the senior or executive level, with the ability to integrate industry insights into teaching. Dedication to promoting an inclusive, equitable, and diverse academic environment. Experience teaching in online or hybrid learning formats. Proven involvement in industry partnerships, consulting projects, or collaborative initiatives. This is a non-tenure track, annually renewable position. This position requires a flexible work schedule that includes being present on the Boston campus, required evening hours and the possibility of weekend hours. Travel to the University’s other campuses may be required. Additional Information: Interested candidates should apply here with a curriculum vita, cover letter and teaching statement addressing the prompt below, and names and contact information for at least three professional references from whom letters of reference can be solicited as needed. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, as they arrive. Successful faculty at Northeastern will be dynamic and innovative scholars with a record of teaching excellence and a commitment to fostering belonging in the university community. Thus, strong candidates for this faculty position will have the expertise, knowledge, and skills to build their pedagogy, and curriculum in ways that reflect and enhance this commitment. Please indicate how your expertise, knowledge, and skills have prepared you to contribute to this work in a teaching statement addressing the following prompt: Teaching statement (1 page): Please summarize your past instructional and mentorship experiences, your pedagogical philosophy, your plans/goals for teaching in the College of Professional Studies (including existing and proposed courses), and your strategies for teaching and mentoring global student populations. Please direct questions to Andrew Kinley, a.kinley@northeastern.edu. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer. Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information. Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: 52-week Salary Ranges: Assistant Teaching Professor: $77,000.00 - $95,000.00 | Associate Teaching Professor: $85,000.00 - $107,000.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Boston-MA-Main-Campus/Outreach--Education---Policy-Manager_R143157": {
      "title": "Outreach, Education & Policy Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary The Outreach, Education & Policy Manager, part of Research Enterprise Services (NU-RES), Research Compliance Team, facilitates the development and deployment of professional and mandated research-related training for research administrators, research staff, and faculty across the Northeastern campus network. In addition, this role is responsible for creating and curating communications and facilitating the successful deployment of research-related policies, including updating procedure documents and communications. The Manager works collaboratively with research compliance, college leadership, and NU-RES staff to promote the effective use of research project management tools and systems, as well as alignment between these systems, practices, and institutional policy. The Manager is responsible for building a comprehensive plan to design, develop, document, and deliver training related to research administration and the continuous improvement of department initiatives. In addition, the Manager works with identified stakeholders to develop and deploy engaging online instructional content for a variety of research administration, finance, and compliance topics. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities Training (40%) Assess and identify training needs for faculty and staff in research administration Partner with internal stakeholders and subject matter experts regarding training needs and instructional design Facilitate learning through a variety of delivery methods, including classroom instruction and virtual training Use software to create online videos and modules in partnership with subject matter experts using University-approved systems Partner with key stakeholders to update online training materials and tools to ensure they are current and correct Provide relevant training metrics and data to leadership to ensure that research trainings are completed Gather feedback on all training delivered and measure effectiveness and satisfaction, as well as recommend mitigations and enhancements to services Design and apply assessment tools to measure effectiveness and summarize evaluation reports to determine the impact of the training Policy (20%) Work with research compliance leadership to ensure that policies are up to date and revised on a routine cadence or as otherwise needed Develop and ensure the execution of critical communications for policy rollouts Ensure that all stakeholders are aware of policy changes and that key documents are updated and revised to support successful policy rollouts Communication (20%) Work with the research compliance team to develop effective and engaging content for the website and newsletters Offer input and guidance on ways to improve communication with key stakeholder groups across the NU-RES enterprise and build rapport with other stakeholder teams to facilitate well-thought-out communication Research Administration Training Program (15%) Build and deploy a comprehensive training plan covering the research administration lifecycle for research administration professionals and related staff across the University, including gathering and executing feedback and continuous improvement Map out training plans and design and develop an in-house training program, including a tiered certificate program Monitor and analyze developments and major issues within the research administration field to share with faculty and staff, as appropriate, through newsletters Manage and lead monthly continuous learning sessions, including Learn More and Brown Bags, including identifying and managing the need for ongoing education and inviting relevant guest speakers Work with Research Compliance leadership to manage the Responsible Conduct of Research series to deliver effective and engaging content geared toward postdoctoral scholars and junior faculty Special Projects (5%) Perform other duties as assigned or special projects to meet the goals of the department and the institution Work with the Research Compliance team to oversee document management, including organizing and curating SharePoint documentation and managing access Minimum Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree in business, research administration, education, communication, project management, instructional design, finance, science, or a related field At least 5–7 years of relevant experience 4–6 years of experience in grants administration 1–2 years of training and development experience, which may be concurrent with grants administration experience Knowledge of grants administration, communications, and instructional design Effective communication, particularly listening, organization, adaptability, and time management skills Preferred Master's degree in business, research administration, education, communication, project management, instructional design, finance, science, or a related field Experience with learning management systems, systems integration or data management, and video design/development Required Documents Resume Position Type Human Resources Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 110S Expected Hiring Range: $76,335.00 - $107,823.75 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change."
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Burlington-MA/Biotechnology-Education-Lab-Technician_R143140": {
      "title": "Biotechnology Education Lab Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Support biotechnology education across Massachusetts while gaining hands-on laboratory experience in molecular biology and genetic engineering! Job Summary We are looking for 2 interns to serve as a lab technician, supporting Amgen Biotech Experience MA biotech education outreach program, its educators and students (1 high school student and 1 post-graduate) In additional to general lab skills, applicant will be expected to partake in a self-directed research project related to the ABE MA content area. Lastly, applicant should also be comfortable with participating in the creation of educational materials and/or supporting communications work, like a social media page/newsletter. What You Will Do Follow SOPs to prepare laboratory reagent stocks and materials Construct customized laboratory reagent and equipment kits for science educators (up to 7 kits/month) Utilize aseptic technique to prepare materials involving bacterial specimens Support delivery of high-quality biotechnology learning experiences across Massachusetts Research Opportunity Design and manage an independent research project related to biotechnology concepts, techniques, or equipment used in ABE MA curricula Choose your own topic or select from provided project ideas Education & Outreach Impact Create an educational activity, classroom resource, or instructional deliverable for participating teachers Contribute tools that help students succeed in biotechnology learning Ideal Candidates Biology, Biotechnology, Biochemistry, Biomedical Sciences, or related students/recent graduates Experience using micropipettes, autoclaves, and gel electrophoresis equipment, with willingness to learn additional equipment. Detail-oriented and organized Able to work independently Comfortable following protocols and safety procedures Interested in laboratory science and experiential STEM education Position Type Temporary Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. This job is for a current or anticipated job vacancy. Pay Rate: $20/hour"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Burlington-MA/Burlington-Campus-Operations---Admin-Coordinator_R143151-1": {
      "title": "Burlington Campus Operations & Admin Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Position Summary The Temporary Campus Operations & Administrative Coordinator provides operational, administrative, and event support for Northeastern University's Burlington Campus. This position serves as a key point of contact for campus stakeholders, visitors, vendors, and service providers, ensuring the smooth coordination of campus activities, conference center operations, facilities requests, and administrative functions. The coordinator will support day-to-day campus operations, special events, visitor engagement, and facility-related activities while maintaining a high level of customer service and responsiveness to faculty, staff, students, research partners, and external guests. This position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment. Essential Responsibilities Administrative & Office Operations Provide access administration for campus Provide administrative support for Burlington campus leadership and campus operations. Manage calendars, meeting schedules, conference room reservations, and campus event calendars. Expense reports, purchasing requests, and invoice processing. Maintain operational records, databases, distribution lists, and filing systems. Assist with onboarding logistics for visitors, guests, and new employees. Support procurement and inventory management of office supplies. Event & Conference Center Management Coordinate meetings, conferences, workshops, seminars, receptions, and special events held on campus. Serve as the primary coordinator for Building 5 conference and event space scheduling. Coordinate room setups, audiovisual requirements, catering, parking, security, and vendor services. Conduct planning meetings and walkthroughs with event organizers. Develop and distribute event schedules and setup requirements to Facilities, Security, and service providers. Provide on-site event support before, during, and after scheduled events. Assist with executive meetings held on campus. Campus Operations & Facilities Coordination Serve as a central point of contact for operational and facility-related requests. Coordinate maintenance requests and communicate with Facilities Management and external vendors. Monitor completion of service requests and follow up with stakeholders as needed. Assist with office moves, space changes, signage requests, and campus logistics. Coordinate vendor access and service scheduling. Prepare and distribute campus operational notices, maintenance communications, and event advisories. Support coordination of visitor parking and general campus services. Visitor Experience & Customer Service Welcome and assist campus visitors, guests, faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Coordinate visitor logistics, reservations, parking arrangements, and meeting support. Respond to questions regarding campus services, conference facilities, and campus operations. Maintain a positive and professional customer service experience for all campus constituents. Communications Support Assist with preparation and distribution of campus communications. Maintain event information, campus announcements, and operational updates. Coordinate communication of campus service disruptions, maintenance activities, and event schedules. Shuttle Service Coordination Serve as the primary administrative contact for the Burlington Campus shuttle service. Communicate shuttle schedules, route updates, delays, and service disruptions to campus stakeholders. Coordinate with shuttle providers regarding service issues and rider concerns. Escalate service interruptions, staffing concerns, vehicle issues, or operational risks to campus leadership for review and decision-making. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree preferred or equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum five years of experience in administrative support, office management, campus operations, event coordination, hospitality, or related fields. Strong organizational and project coordination skills. Excellent written and verbal communication abilities. Demonstrated customer service experience. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines independently. Proficiency with Microsoft Office 365, including Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Teams. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education, research, healthcare, or corporate campus environments. Experience coordinating conferences, meetings, and special events. Experience working with facilities vendors and contractors. Experience supporting executive-level meetings and visitors. Experience using room scheduling, event management, or facilities management systems. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Exceptional attention to detail. Strong interpersonal and relationship management skills. Ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment. Strong problem-solving and organizational skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism. Ability to adapt to changing priorities in a fast-paced environment.   Position Type Temporary Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. This job is for a current or anticipated job vacancy. Pay Rate: 32.00 - 37.00 hourly rate"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/New-York-NY/Part-Time-Lecturer---Department-of-Physical-Therapy--Movement--and-Rehabilitation-Sciences---New-York-campus_R143150": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer - Department of Physical Therapy, Movement, and Rehabilitation Sciences - New York campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nPart time\n\nAbout the Opportunity About the Opportunity Part-time Instructor positions available as determined by department’s curricular and institutional needs to teach in undergraduate and graduate courses in the Department of Physical Therapy, Movement, and Rehabilitation Sciences, New York City campus. Responsibilities include : Development and administration of lecture, recitation, and/or laboratory experiences for PT 1880: Introduction to Sport Medicine (Spring 2027); with the potential to teach more courses dependent on evaluation of teaching; Preparation of lectures, course materials, examinations, and evaluation of student performance in the course; Part-time instructors will hold office hours (2-3 hours weekly) including but not limited to group and individual tutoring; Part-time instructors will report to the Department of Physical Therapy, Movement, and Rehabilitation Science (PTMRS) Department Chair. Qualifications :  A graduate degree in a Kinesiology-related field is required. Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) or APTA Clinical Specialist Certification or Board Certification Athletic Trainer (ATC) is preferred. Successful applicants will have work experience and college teaching experience in undergraduate, diverse higher education institution or clinical instructor experience.   Additional Information : The Department of Physical Therapy, Movement, and Rehabilitation Sciences (PTMRS) at Northeastern is founded on the university’s core values of interdisciplinary education, urban engagement, international knowledge, and cutting-edge research. The PTMRS Department Mission is to impact the health and well-being of the global community by developing leaders in physical therapy, movement, and rehabilitation through interprofessional, experiential education, translational research, and excellence in clinical practice. Our exceptional faculty are dedicated to promoting excellence in practice, education, scholarship, and community service. Faculty are engaged in active clinical research and practice. A hallmark of our program is the integration of experiential learning and didactic education whether through use of standardized patients, communication and interaction with community consultants, participation in service learning projects, or engagement in research with our faculty. Graduates from Northeastern are innovative, global leaders who excel in clinical practice, research and community service. As one of the longest accredited programs in the United States, and the only program with Cooperative Education, our students graduate with exceptional clinical decision-making skills, and experience in the fields of physical therapy, kinesiology, dance medicine, and human movement science. Northeastern University will not provide H-1B, TN, O-1, E-3, or any other type of employment visa sponsorship for the successful applicant to this position, now or in the future.  STEM OPT is not compatible for this position. The successful applicant must be able to maintain valid work authorization in the United States throughout the entire appointment without Northeastern University's sponsorship for a visa.  Position Type Academic Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Pay Range: The rate per credit is $1,571.10"
    },
    "https://northeastern.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/careers/job/Vancouver-BC-Canada/Wellness-Program-Specialist_R143137": {
      "title": "Wellness Program Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nAbout the Opportunity Job Summary: The Wellness Program Specialist position will support the wellness of learners at Northeastern’s Vancouver campus. This is an 18 month term appointment. The Specialist will develop and deliver a proactive wellness programming plan for students, addressing all dimensions of wellness, both by scaling and tailoring resources already available at Northeastern, and by researching and connecting to local resources in Vancouver. The Specialist will work collaboratively with Vancouver staff as well as staff at global campuses to tailor wellness programming appropriately and reach the widest audience. The Specialist will support learners by providing resources, referrals, and guidance to help the learner develop healthy wellness practices, as well as overcome wellness challenges. They will serve as a case manager for students in crisis at Northeastern Vancouver, including situations related to Title IX, mental and physical health, and student emergencies, ensuring follow up and continual support. Support includes but is not limited to referrals to Northeastern departments such as University Health & Counseling Services and the Disability Access Services, as well as local resources in the learner’s community. The Specialist will be responsible for data tracking and analysis. He/she/they will track engagement with wellness programming, trainings, cases, and communications, identify trends, and offer suggestions to improve services, programs and processes. This position carries significant responsibility because of the time sensitive information that must be accurately conveyed to all customers. This is a highly visible position requiring constant and high-caliber customer contact via telephone, e-mail and in-person visitors, and the ability to provide assistance through the point of problem resolution. The Wellness Program Specialist must be comfortable working in a very fast-paced environment. He/She/They must possess the ability to handle confidential information in a sensitive manner; be detailed oriented; possess strong administrative experience and communicate clearly and effectively to a diverse student population. Additionally, they must possess enthusiasm for wellness and higher education and a commitment to the mission and goals of the University through his/her/their dedication to customer service. The Wellness Program Specialist may be expected to be available by phone after hours and available some nights and weekends as needed. Responsibilities Include: Develop and deliver wellness programming plan for students, prioritizing students’ mental, physical, emotional wellbeing through their academic journeys. Serve as case manager for students in crisis including Title IX, mental health, and student emergencies ensuring follow up and continual support. Track engagement with wellness programming, trainings, and student response, including utilization and trends, and create reports to measure and improve services. Manage annual comprehensive wellness survey and analyze survey results to identify student trends and satisfaction and extrapolate strategic recommendations to address. Minimum Qualifications Employee must have the flexibility to work on several projects concurrently. Demonstrated diplomacy and sensitivity in working with confidential matters. Sound judgement and analytical skills; attention to detail with a high degree of accuracy and follow-through; ability to work under pressure with a positive attitude. Ability to work independently as well as part of a team. Ability to work effectively in a culturally diverse environment and possess enthusiasm for higher education and have an overall commitment to excellence in customer service. Outgoing, detail-oriented team player who is able to communicate clearly to a diverse student, parent, and staff population. Ability to multi-task in a fast-paced, high traffic environment. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential materials. Willingness and ability to adapt and learn quickly new policies and procedures. Knowledge and skills required are typically obtained through a bachelor’s required plus at least 2-4 years’ experience in College/University setting or a related field, ideally in wellness programming and student services/student life. Position Type Student Services Additional Information Northeastern University considers factors such as candidate work experience, education and skills when extending an offer.   Northeastern has a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees. This includes medical, vision, dental, paid time off, tuition assistance, wellness & life, retirement- as well as commuting & transportation. Visit https://hr.northeastern.edu/benefits/ for more information.    All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, sexual orientation, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Compensation Grade/Pay Type: 107S Expected Hiring Range: $63,265.00 - $98,060.00 With the pay range(s) shown above, the starting salary will depend on several factors, which may include your education, experience, location, knowledge and expertise, and skills as well as a pay comparison to similarly-situated employees already in the role. Salary ranges are reviewed regularly and are subject to change.   Applicant must be legally entitled to work in Canada for the duration of the appointment or employment without employer sponsorship."
    }
  },
